// # Architecture Overview
// 
// This document provides a comprehensive overview of the CodeEditorLand
// architecture, component interactions, and design principles.
// 
// ## 📑 Table of Contents
// 
// - [Architecture Principles](#architecture-principles)
// - [Component Overview](#component-overview)
// - [System Architecture](#system-architecture)
// - [Communication Flows](#communication-flows)
// - [Deployment Models](#deployment-models)
// - [Technology Stack](#technology-stack)
// 
// ## Architecture Principles
// 
// ### 1. Modularity
// 
// Each component in CodeEditorLand is designed to be independently developed,
// tested, and deployed:
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "Component 1"
//         C1[Component A]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Component 2"
//         C2[Component B]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Component 3"
//         C3[Component C]
//     end
// 
//     C1 -- "Vine Protocol" --> C2
//     C2 -- "Vine Protocol" --> C3
//     C3 -- "Vine Protocol" --> C1
// ```
// 
// **Benefits:**
// 
// - Reduced coupling between components
// - Independent versioning and deployment
// - Clear ownership boundaries
// - Easier testing and maintenance
// 
// ### 2. Protocol Abstraction
// 
// All communication flows through Vine, the unified protocol layer:
// 
// ```mermaid
// sequenceDiagram
//     participant UI as Sky (UI)
//     participant Vine as Vine (Protocol)
//     participant EH as Cocoon/Grove
//     participant BE as Mountain
// 
//     UI->>Vine: Request
//     Vine->>Vine: Serialize/Validate
//     Vine->>EH: Forward Request
//     EH->>EH: Process Request
//     EH-->>Vine: Response
//     Vine->>Vine: Deserialize/Validate
//     Vine-->>UI: Response
// ```
// 
// **Benefits:**
// 
// - Transport-agnostic communication
// - Language-independent protocol
// - Version-controlled interfaces
// - Multiple transport options
// 
// ### 3. Extensibility
// 
// Two extension host environments support different extension types:
// 
// ```mermaid
// flowchart LR
//     subgraph "Extension Hosts"
//         C[🦋 Cocoon<br/>Node.js]
//         G[🌲 Grove<br/>Rust/WASM]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Extension Types"
//         JS[JS/TS Extensions]
//         RS[Rust Extensions]
//         WASM[WASM Extensions]
//     end
// 
//     C --> JS
//     G --> RS
//     G --> WASM
// 
//     C --> G
//     G --> C
// ```
// 
// ## Component Overview
// 
// | Component    | Symbol | Role              | Technology         | Status     |
// | ------------ | ------ | ----------------- | ------------------ | ---------- |
// | **Cocoon**   | 🦋     | Extension Host    | Node.js            | ✅ Active  |
// | **Grove**    | 🌲     | Extension Host    | Rust + WASM        | 🔄 Planned |
// | **Mountain** | 🏔️     | Native Backend    | Tauri + Rust       | ✅ Active  |
// | **Vine**     | 🌿     | Protocol Layer    | Protocol Buffers   | ✅ Active  |
// | **Air**      | 💨     | Background Daemon | Rust               | 🔄 Planned |
// | **Wind**     | 🌬️     | UI Service        | Rust               | 🔄 Planned |
// | **Sky**      | ☁️     | UI Components     | Astro + TypeScript | ✅ Active  |
// 
// ## System Architecture
// 
// ### High-Level Architecture
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "Frontend Layer"
//         UI[☁️ Sky UI<br/>Astro Components]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "UI Service Layer"
//         Service[🌬️ Wind<br/>UI Service]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Protocol Layer"
//         Protocol[🌿 Vine<br/>Protocol Definition]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Transport Layer"
//         gRPC[gRPC Transport]
//         IPC[IPC Transport]
//         WASM[WASM Transport]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Extension Host Layer"
//         Cocoon[🦋 Cocoon<br/>Node.js Host]
//         Grove[🌲 Grove<br/>Rust/WASM Host]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Backend Layer"
//         Mountain[🏔️ Mountain<br/>Native Backend]
//         Air[💨 Air<br/>Background Daemon]
//     end
// 
//     UI --> Service
//     Service --> Protocol
//     Protocol --> gRPC
//     Protocol --> IPC
//     Protocol --> WASM
// 
//     gRPC --> Cocoon
//     gRPC --> Grove
//     IPC --> Cocoon
//     IPC --> Grove
//     WASM --> Grove
// 
//     Cocoon --> Mountain
//     Grove --> Mountain
//     Cocoon --> Air
//     Grove --> Air
// ```
// 
// ### Component Interactions
// 
// #### Frontend to Backend Flow
// 
// ```mermaid
// sequenceDiagram
//     participant User as User
//     participant UI as Sky (UI)
//     participant Wind as Wind (Service)
//     participant Vine as Vine (Protocol)
//     participant transport as Transport
//     participant Cocoon as Cocoon (EH)
//     participant Mountain as Mountain (Backend)
// 
//     User->>UI: User Action
//     UI->>Wind: Request
//     Wind->>Vine: Serialize Request
//     Vine->>transport: Send via Transport
//     transport->>Cocoon: Receive Request
//     Cocoon->>Cocoon: Execute Extension
//     Cocoon->>Mountain: Backend Operation
//     Mountain-->>Cocoon: Result
//     Cocoon-->>transport: Response
//     transport-->>Vine: Deserialize Response
//     Vine-->>Wind: Response
//     Wind-->>UI: Update UI
//     UI-->>User: Display Result
// ```
// 
// #### Extension Loading Flow
// 
// ```mermaid
// sequenceDiagram
//     participant System as System
//     participant Mountain as Mountain (Backend)
//     participant Cocoon as Cocoon (EH)
//     participant Extension as Extension
// 
//     System->>Mountain: Start
//     Mountain->>Mountain: Load Config
//     Mountain->>Cocoon: Initialize Host
//     Cocoon->>Extension: Load Extension
//     Extension-->>Cocoon: Ready
//     Cocoon-->>Mountain: Extension Available
//     Mountain-->>System: Ready
// ```
// 
// ## Communication Flows
// 
// ### Request Lifecycle
// 
// ```mermaid
// stateDiagram-v2
//     [*] --> Pending: User Action
//     Pending --> Validating: Sky UI
//     Validating --> Serializing: Wind Service
//     Serializing --> Transporting: Vine Protocol
//     Transporting --> Processing: Extension Host
//     Processing --> Executing: Extension
// 
//    Executing --> BackendOp: Need Backend?
//     Executing --> Response: No Backend Needed
// 
//     BackendOp --> Response: Backend Complete
// 
//     Response --> Deserializing: Vine Protocol
//     Deserializing --> Rendering: Wind Service
//     Rendering --> Complete: Sky UI
//     Complete --> [*]
// ```
// 
// ### Error Handling Flow
// 
// ```mermaid
// flowchart TD
//     Request[Request] --> Try{Try Execute}
//     Try --> Success[Success]
//     Try --> Error[Error]
// 
//     Error --> Catch{Catch Error}
//     Catch --> Extension{Extension Error?}
//     Catch --> Protocol{Protocol Error?}
//     Catch --> Transport{Transport Error?}
// 
//     Extension --> Log[Log Error]
//     Protocol --> Log
//     Transport --> Log
// 
//     Log --> Recover{Can Recover?}
//     Recover --> Yes[Retry/Fallback]
//     Recover --> No[User Error]
// 
//     Yes --> Try
//     No --> Display[Display to User]
//     Display --> Done[Done]
//     Success --> Done
// ```
// 
// ## Deployment Models
// 
// ### Model 1: Desktop Application (Tauri)
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "Single Process (Tauri)"
//         UI[☁️ Sky UI]
//         Wind[🌬️ Wind Service]
//         Vine[🌿 Vine]
//         Cocoon[🦋 Cocoon]
//         Mountain[🏔️ Mountain]
//     end
// 
//     UI --> Wind
//     Wind --> Vine
//     Vine --> Cocoon
//     Cocoon --> Mountain
// ```
// 
// **Characteristics:**
// 
// - Single executable
// - Native performance
// - Local file system access
// - IPC transport preferred
// 
// ### Model 2: Distributed Desktop
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "Frontend Process"
//         UI[☁️ Sky UI]
//         Wind[🌬️ Wind Service]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Extension Process"
//         Cocoon[🦋 Cocoon]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Backend Process"
//         Mountain[🏔️ Mountain]
//         Air[💨 Air Daemon]
//     end
// 
//     UI --> Wind
//     Wind -->|gRPC| Cocoon
//     Cocoon -->|gRPC| Mountain
//     Mountain --> Air
// ```
// 
// **Characteristics:**
// 
// - Multiple processes
// - gRPC transport
// - Better isolation
// - Crash recovery
// 
// ### Model 3: Web Application
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "Browser"
//         UI[☁️ Sky UI]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Web Server"
//         Wind[🌬️ Wind Service]
//         Grove[🌲 Grove]
//     end
// 
//     UI -->|WASM/WebSocket| Wind
//     Wind --> Grove
// ```
// 
// **Characteristics:**
// 
// - Pure web deployment
// - WASM transport
// - Browser constraints
// - Cloud backend possible
// 
// ## Technology Stack
// 
// ### Core Technologies
// 
// | Layer                 | Technology              | Purpose               |
// | --------------------- | ----------------------- | --------------------- |
// | **Protocol**          | Protocol Buffers        | Schema definition     |
// | **Transport: gRPC**   | gRPC + HTTP/2           | Remote communication  |
// | **Transport: IPC**    | Native IPC              | Local communication   |
// | **Transport: WASM**   | WebAssembly + WebSocket | Browser communication |
// | **Backend: Mountain** | Tauri + Rust            | Desktop backend       |
// | **Extension: Cocoon** | Node.js                 | JavaScript extensions |
// | **Extension: Grove**  | Rust + WASM             | Native extensions     |
// | **Frontend: Sky**     | Astro + TypeScript      | User interface        |
// 
// ### Supporting Technologies
// 
// | Category          | Technology            | Purpose            |
// | ----------------- | --------------------- | ------------------ |
// | **Build**         | Cargo, rsbuild, Astro | Build systems      |
// | **Testing**       | Vitest, Rust Test     | Testing frameworks |
// | **Linting**       | ESLint, Clippy        | Code quality       |
// | **Formatting**    | Prettier, rustfmt     | Code formatting    |
// | **Documentation** | Mermaid, MDX          | Documentation      |
// 
// ## Design Patterns
// 
// ### Strategy Pattern
// 
// Applied to transport selection:
// 
// ```mermaid
// classDiagram
//     class Transport {
//         <<interface>>
//         +send(request)
//         +receive(response)
//     }
// 
//     class GRPCTransport {
//         +send(request)
//         +receive(response)
//     }
// 
//     class IPCTransport {
//         +send(request)
//         +receive(response)
//     }
// 
//     class WASMTransport {
//         +send(request)
//         +receive(response)
//     }
// 
//     class TransportFactory {
//         +create(type) Transport
//     }
// 
//     Transport <|.. GRPCTransport
//     Transport <|.. IPCTransport
//     Transport <|.. WASMTransport
//     TransportFactory --> Transport
// ```
// 
// ### Observer Pattern
// 
// Applied to UI updates:
// 
// ```mermaid
// classDiagram
//     class Subject {
//         +attach(observer)
//         +detach(observer)
//         +notify(event)
//     }
// 
//     class Observer {
//         <<interface>>
//         +update(event)
//     }
// 
//     class WindService {
//         +attach(observer)
//         +detach(observer)
//         +notify(event)
//     }
// 
//     class SkyUI {
//         +update(event)
//     }
// 
//     Subject <|.. WindService
//     Observer <|.. SkyUI
// ```
// 
// ### Factory Pattern
// 
// Applied to extension instantiation:
// 
// ```mermaid
// classDiagram
//     class ExtensionFactory {
//         <<interface>>
//         +create(config) Extension
//     }
// 
//     class JSExtensionFactory {
//         +create(config) JSExtension
//     }
// 
//     class RustExtensionFactory {
//         +create(config) RustExtension
//     }
// 
//     class Extension {
//         <<interface>>
//         +execute(request)
//     }
// 
//     ExtensionFactory <|.. JSExtensionFactory
//     ExtensionFactory <|.. RustExtensionFactory
//     JSExtensionFactory ..> JSExtension
//     RustExtensionFactory ..> RustExtension
//     Extension <|.. JSExtension
//     Extension <|.. RustExtension
// ```
// 
// ## Security Considerations
// 
// ### Extension Sandboxing
// 
// ```mermaid
// flowchart LR
//     subgraph "Safe Zone"
//         UI[UI Components]
//         Wind[UI Service]
//         Mountain[Backend]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Sandbox Zone"
//         Cocoon[Cocoon Host]
//         Grove[Grove Host]
//     end
// 
//     UI -->|Vine Protocol| Cocoon
//     UI -->|Vine Protocol| Grove
//     Wind -->|Vine Protocol| Cocoon
//     Wind -->|Vine Protocol| Grove
// 
//     Cocoon -->|Restricted API| Mountain
//     Grove -->|Restricted API| Mountain
// 
//     subgraph "Protected Resources"
//         File[File System]
//         Network[Network]
//         Process[Processes]
//     end
// 
//     Mountain --> File
//     Mountain --> Network
//     Mountain --> Process
// ```
// 
// ### Permission Model
// 
// | Permission         | Description       | Default |
// | ------------------ | ----------------- | ------- |
// | `fs:read`          | Read files        | Deny    |
// | `fs:write`         | Write files       | Deny    |
// | `network:outbound` | Outbound network  | Prompt  |
// | `network:inbound`  | Inbound network   | Deny    |
// | `process:execute`  | Execute processes | Deny    |
// | `ui:modify`        | Modify UI         | Allow   |
// 
// ## Performance Considerations
// 
// ### Optimization Strategies
// 
// 1. **Transport Selection**
//     - Use IPC for same-process communication
//     - Use gRPC for cross-process communication
//     - Use WASM for browser scenarios
// 
// 2. **Caching**
//     - Extension metadata caching
//     - UI component caching
//     - Protocol message caching
// 
// 3. **Lazy Loading**
//     - Extensions loaded on demand
//     - UI components loaded as needed
//     - Backend services initialized lazily
// 
// 4. **Parallel Processing**
//     - Concurrent extension execution
//     - Async UI updates
//     - Parallel backend operations
// 
// ## Future Enhancements
// 
// ### Planned Features
// 
// - [ ] Multi-instance support
// - [ ] Extension hot-reload
// - [ ] Distributed backend
// - [ ] Cloud synchronization
// - [ ] AI-assisted development
// - [ ] Real-time collaboration
// 
// ### Research Areas
// 
// - WebGPU acceleration
// - WebRTC for collaboration
// - Distributed file systems
// - Edge computing integration
// 
