// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// # API Categories
// 
// Detailed documentation for each API namespace in the unified CodeEditorLand API
// surface.
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// This directory contains comprehensive documentation for each API namespace,
// including:
// 
// - **Method signatures and descriptions**
// - **Implementation status across variants** (color-coded)
// - **Type definitions and interfaces**
// - **Event specifications**
// - **Code examples in TypeScript and Rust**
// - **Cross-references to related components**
// 
// ## Available Categories
// 
// | Category                                                                                                 | Description                                                           | Documentation                          | Status                                         |
// | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
// | [`Workspace API`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/workspace.md) | File system, configuration, workspace folders, text documents         | <span style="color:white">Ready</span> | <span style="color:white">Complete</span>      |
// | [`Window API`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/window.md)       | UI elements, messages, dialogs, terminals, status bars                | <span style="color:white">Ready</span> | <span style="color:white">Complete</span>      |
// | [`Commands API`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/commands.md)   | Command registration and execution                                    | <span style="color:white">Ready</span> | <span style="color:white">Complete</span>      |
// | [`Languages API`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/languages.md) | Language providers and features (hover, completion, definition, etc.) | <span style="color:white">Ready</span> | <span style="color:#64b6ff">In Progress</span> |
// | [`Debug API`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/debug.md)         | Debug adapter protocol integration, breakpoints, debug console        | <span style="color:white">Ready</span> | <span style="color:#64b6ff">In Progress</span> |
// | [`SCM API`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/scm.md)             | Source control management, resource groups, operations                | <span style="color:white">Ready</span> | <span style="color:#64b6ff">In Progress</span> |
// | [`Terminal API`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/terminal.md)   | Terminal integration, process management, dimensions                  | <span style="color:white">Ready</span> | <span style="color:white">Complete</span>      |
// | [`Environment API`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/env.md)     | Environment variables, app info, clipboard, shell                     | <span style="color:white">Ready</span> | <span style="color:white">Complete</span>      |
// 
// ## Documentation Structure
// 
// Each category document follows a consistent structure:
// 
// ### 1. Overview
// 
// - Brief description of the namespace's purpose
// - When and why to use this API
// - Key concepts and terminology
// 
// ### 2. Architecture Diagram
// 
// - Mermaid diagram showing the namespace structure
// - Component relationships and data flow
// 
// ### 3. API Methods Reference
// 
// Comprehensive table with:
// 
// - Method name and signature
// - Parameters and return types
// - Implementation status by variant (color-coded)
// - Usage notes and caveats
// 
// | Method     | Signature              | Cocoon | Grove | Mountain | Wind | Sky | Status |
// | ---------- | ---------------------- | ------ | ----- | -------- | ---- | --- | ------ |
// | methodName | (params) => ReturnType | ✅     | 🔄    | ❌       | ✅   | ✅  | Ready  |
// 
// ### 4. Data Types and Interfaces
// 
// - Type definitions for TypeScript
// - Struct and trait definitions for Rust
// - Type compatibility notes
// 
// ### 5. Events
// 
// - Event types and when they fire
// - Event data payload specification
// - Event availability by variant
// 
// | Event     | Trigger     | Data           | Availability             |
// | --------- | ----------- | -------------- | ------------------------ |
// | eventName | Description | Data structure | Color-coded availability |
// 
// ### 6. TypeScript Code Examples
// 
// - Practical usage examples
// - Common patterns and best practices
// - Extension integration samples
// 
// ### 7. Rust Code Examples
// 
// - Rust-specific implementations
// - Error handling patterns
// - Async/await usage
// 
// ### 8. Cross-Variant Notes
// 
// - Variant-specific behavior differences
// - Spine integration considerations
// - Fallback patterns for missing features
// 
// ### 9. Related Documentation
// 
// - Links to component documentation
// - Links to workflow examples
// - Links to API contracts
// 
// ## Color Coding Legend
// 
// | Status                                        | Color | Meaning                                          |
// | --------------------------------------------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------ |
// | <span style="color:white">✅ Ready</span>     | White | Implemented and working across relevant variants |
// | <span style="color:#64b6ff">🔄 Planned</span> | Blue  | Pending implementation or future work            |
// | ❌ Not Supported                              | Red   | Not applicable to this variant                   |
// 
// ## Usage Guide
// 
// ### For Extension Developers
// 
// 1. **Start with the category overview** to understand the namespace's purpose
// 2. **Review the API methods table** to find the methods you need
// 3. **Check implementation status** to ensure compatibility with your target
//    variants
// 4. **Study the code examples** to understand proper usage patterns
// 5. **Reference related documentation** for deeper context
// 
// ### For Variant Maintainers
// 
// 1. **Use the method tables** to track implementation progress
// 2. **Update color-coded status** as you implement features
// 3. **Add variant-specific notes** to document differences
// 4. **Include code examples** demonstrating variant-specific patterns
// 
// ## Quick Reference
// 
// ### Core Categories (Essential for Most Extensions)
// 
// - **[`workspace`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/workspace.md)** -
//   File operations, configuration, workspace folders
// - **[`window`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/window.md)** -
//   User interaction, messages, dialogs
// - **[`commands`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/commands.md)** -
//   Command registration and execution
// 
// ### Advanced Categories
// 
// - **[`languages`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/languages.md)** -
//   Language features (completion, hover, definition)
// - **[`debug`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/debug.md)** -
//   Debugging capabilities
// - **[`scm`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/scm.md)** -
//   Source control integration
// 
// ### Supporting Categories
// 
// - **[`terminal`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/terminal.md)** -
//   Terminal integration
// - **[`env`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/api/categories/env.md)** -
//   Environment and system information
