// plans/plans/api/compatibility/README.md
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// # Compatibility Documentation
// 
// Overview of cross-variant compatibility and migration guides for CodeEditorLand variants.
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// This directory contains documentation for ensuring compatibility across all CodeEditorLand variants:
// 
// - **Cocoon** - TypeScript-based VS Code extension host
// - **Grove** - Rust-based native application
// - **Mountain** - Backend services
// - **Wind** - Lightweight embedded runtime
// - **Sky** - Web-based runtime
// 
// ## Compatibility Guides
// 
// | Guide | Description | Status |
// |-------|-------------|--------|
// | [Cocoon vs Grove API Compatibility](cocoon-grove-api-compat.md) | TypeScript to Rust API mapping and migration guide | <span style="color:white">Ready</span> |
// | [Mountain Backend Bridging](mountain-backend-bridging.md) | Backend service bridging patterns and Spine integration | <span style="color:white">Ready</span> |
// 
// ## Key Compatibility Concepts
// 
// ### 1. API Surface Consistency
// 
// All variants implement a unified API surface with consistent method signatures and behavior, regardless of the underlying implementation language.
// 
// ### 2. Type Mapping
// 
// TypeScript and Rust types map to each other through the unified interface:
// 
// | TypeScript Type | Rust Type | Notes |
// |----------------|-----------|-------|
// | `string` | `String`, `&str` | Use `Cow<'_, str>` for flexible ownership |
// | `number` | `f64`, `i32`, `u32` | Context-dependent |
// | `boolean` | `bool` | Direct mapping |
// | `Promise<T>` | `impl Future<Output = Result<T>>` | Async operations |
// | `Disposable` | `Box<dyn Disposable>` | Trait objects |
// | `URI` | `Uri` | Custom type with conversion methods |
// 
// ### 3. Event System
// 
// - **TypeScript**: Uses EventEmitter pattern with callbacks
// - **Rust**: Uses tokio channels for event streaming
// 
// ### 4. Error Handling
// 
// - **TypeScript**: Uses `try/catch` and Promise rejections
// - **Rust**: Uses `Result<T, E>` and the `?` operator
// 
// ## Spine Integration
// 
// The Spine protocol enables variants to communicate with Mountain backend services:
// 
// ### Spine Request Pattern
// 
// ```typescript
// // TypeScript variant sending Spine request
// async function sendSpineRequest(method: string, params: any) {
//     const response = await spine.sendRequest({
//         method,
//         params,
//         id: generateRequestId()
//     });
//     return response.result;
// }
// ```
// 
// ```rust
// // Rust variant sending Spine request
// async fn send_spine_request(method: &str, params: serde_json::Value) -> Result<serde_json::Value> {
//     let request = SpineRequest {
//         method: method.to_string(),
//         params,
//         id: generate_request_id(),
//     };
//     let response = spine.send_request(request).await?;
//     Ok(response.result)
// }
// ```
// 
// ### Fallback Pattern
// 
// When a variant doesn't implement a feature locally, it can fall back to backend services:
// 
// ```typescript
// class BackendAwareWorkspace implements WorkspaceAPI {
//     async readFile Configure/
// │   └── Service/
// ├── Logging/                   # Logging services
// ├── Metrics/                   # Metrics collection (basic)
// ├── Plugins/                   # Plugin system
// ├── Resilience/                # Resilience handling(uri: URI):
// ├── Promise<Uint8Array> { Security/
//         try {
//             return                  # Security services await this.local.readFile
// ├(uri);
//         } catch (localError── Tracing/) {
//             return await this.spine                   # Distributed.request('workspace/read tracing (basic)File', { uri });
//         }
// ├── Updates
//     }
// }
// ```
// 
// ## Compatibility/                   # Update Matrix
// 
// | Feature | Cocoon | management
// └ Grove | Mountain |── Vine/ Wind | Sky | Notes |
// |---------                      # Vine|--------|-------|----------|------ protocol
//     ├──|------|------- Server/
//     │|
// | File System | ✅ |   └── 🔄 | 🔄 | ✅ AirVineg | ✅ |RPCService.rs Via Spine or direct |
// | Configuration
//     └── | ✅ | Generated/
// 
// Status: 🔄 | 🔄 | ✅ 🔄 Core | ✅ | Local and remote | services complete
// | Commands | ✅ | 🔄 | 🔄 |, indexing needs optimization ✅ | ✅ | Command registry
// ```
// 
// ### Task |
// | Language Features 1.4 | 🔄 | 🔄 |: Create detailed implementation ❌ | 🔄 roadmap | 🔄 | LSP integration |
// 
// **Status**: In
// | Debugging | Progress ( 🔄 | ❌ | ❌This document) | 🔄 | 🔄 | D
// 
// **DeliverablesAP integration |
// |**:
// - SCM | 🔄 | 🔄 | ✅ Component 🔄 | structure analysis 🔄 | 🔄 | Git integration |
// - ✅
