// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// # VSCode Rest Compiler Integration Plan
// 
// > **Document Type:** Architecture & Integration Plan  
// > **Created:** 2026-03-06  
// > **Status:** Draft  
// > **Related:** [`docs/vscode-rest-compiler-gap-analysis.md`](../docs/vscode-rest-compiler-gap-analysis.md)
// 
// ---
// 
// ## 1. Executive Summary
// 
// This document provides a comprehensive analysis of the VSCode build process and
// the integration pathway for the Rest compiler to achieve full VSCode compilation
// within the CodeEditorLand ecosystem.
// 
// ### 1.1 Key Findings
// 
// | Component          | Current State                   | Target State                     | Gap                     |
// | ------------------ | ------------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------------- |
// | **Compiler**       | esbuild (primary)               | Rest (Rust/SWC-based)            | Module format, bundling |
// | **Output Dir**     | `Configuration/`                | `Target/Rest/Microsoft/VSCode/`  | Directory structure     |
// | **Build Pipeline** | 2-stage (VSCode → out → Output) | 3-stage (VSCode → Rest → Output) | Rest orchestration      |
// | **Environment**    | `Compiler=esbuild` (default)    | `Compiler=Rest` (opt-in)         | Configuration           |
// 
// ### 1.2 Integration Strategy
// 
// The integration follows a **hybrid approach**:
// 
// - **Rest compiler** handles TypeScript → JavaScript transpilation with SWC
// - **esbuild** continues to handle bundling, tree-shaking, and minification
// - **Output package** orchestrates the pipeline and manages artifact placement
// 
// ---
// 
// ## 2. VSCode Build Process Analysis
// 
// ### 2.1 Source Structure
// 
// ```
// Dependency/Microsoft/Dependency/Editor/
// ├── src/                    # TypeScript source
// │   ├── vscode/            # Core VSCode implementation
// │   ├── base/              # Base utilities
// │   ├── browser/           # Browser-specific code
// │   └── server/            # Server/Node code
// ├── out/                   # TypeScript compilation output (tsc)
// │   ├── vscode/            # Compiled JavaScript
// │   └── ...
// ├── out-build/             # Post-processed output (production)
// └── build/                 # Build scripts and gulp tasks
// ```
// 
// ### 2.2 VSCode Compilation Pipeline
// 
// ```mermaid
// flowchart TD
//     A[TypeScript Source src/] -->|tsc| B[JavaScript out/]
//     B -->|Gulp tasks| C[Post-processing]
//     C -->|NLS, AMD transform| D[out-build/]
//     D -->|Copy/Process| E[Final Output]
// ```
// 
// ### 2.3 Key Build Scripts
// 
// | File                | Purpose                  | Status                   |
// | ------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------ |
// | `package.json`      | Build scripts definition | 🔒 Blocked by .rooignore |
// | `gulpfile.mjs`      | Gulp task orchestration  | 🔒 Blocked by .rooignore |
// | `scripts/*.sh`      | Helper scripts           | 🔒 Blocked by .rooignore |
// | `src/tsconfig.json` | TypeScript configuration | 🔒 Blocked by .rooignore |
// 
// ### 2.4 VSCode Build Stages
// 
