// 
// ## API Signature Notes
// 
// ### Common Differences
// 
// 1. **URI Handling**
//     - VS Code uses `vscode.Uri`
//     - CodeEditorLand uses the same interface
//     - Path operations use the same API
// 
// 2. **Cancellation Tokens**
//     - VS Code uses `CancellationToken`
//     - CodeEditorLand uses `AbortSignal`
//     - Adapter layer provides compatibility
// 
// 3. **Disposable Pattern**
//     - VS Code uses `Disposable` and `Disposable.from()`
//     - CodeEditorLand maintains the same pattern
//     - Full compatibility
// 
// 4. **Range & Position**
//     - VS Code uses `Range` and `Position`
//     - CodeEditorLand uses the same types
//     - Full compatibility
// 
// ### Breaking Changes to Avoid
// 
// | Area              | VS Code Pattern       | CodeEditorLand Implementation |
// | ----------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------- |
// | **File Paths**    | `fsPath` property     | ✅ Preserve `fsPath`          |
// | **Document EOL**  | `eol` enum            | ✅ Use same enum values       |
// | **Language IDs**  | Standard language IDs | ✅ Use same IDs               |
// | **Event Emitter** | `Event<T>` type       | ✅ Compatible type            |
// | **Configuration** | Section-based config  | ✅ Maintain section hierarchy |
// 
