// # Bootstrap File Mapping
// 
// Comprehensive mapping of VS Code bootstrap files to CodeEditorLand equivalents,
// comparing initialization patterns and architecture.
// 
// ## 📑 Table of Contents
// 
// - [Overview](#overview)
// - [Bootstrap File Mapping Table](#bootstrap-file-mapping-table)
// - [Architecture Comparison](#architecture-comparison)
// - [Detailed File Analysis](#detailed-file-analysis)
// - [Initialization Flow](#initialization-flow)
// - [Migration Guide](#migration-guide)
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// VS Code uses a sophisticated bootstrap system that initializes the
// editor在不同 contexts (CLI, Electron, Server). This document maps these patterns
// to CodeEditorLand's multi-component architecture.
// 
// ### Bootstrap Purposes
// 
// | Purpose             | VS Code             | CodeEditorLand   | Description                           |
// | ------------------- | ------------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------- |
// | **CLI Entry**       | `bootstrap-cli.ts`  | Mountain CLI     | Command-line interface initialization |
// | **ESM Setup**       | `bootstrap-esm.ts`  | Grove/Sky ESM    | Module system configuration           |
// | **Process Forking** | `bootstrap-fork.ts` | Cocoon Fork      | Extension host process management     |
// | **Node Utilities**  | `bootstrap-node.ts` | Cocoon Runtime   | Node.js environment setup             |
// | **Main Entry**      | `main.ts`           | Mountain Main    | Desktop application entry point       |
// | **Server Entry**    | `server-main.ts`    | Wind Server mode | Standalone server initialization      |
// 
// ## Bootstrap File Mapping Table
// 
// | VS Code File          | Purpose                    | CodeEditorLand Equivalent Location    | Implementation Status | Notes                               |
// | --------------------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
// | `bootstrap-cli.ts`    | CLI environment cleanup    | `Mountain/Source/CLI/Bootstrap.rs`    | 🟡 Partial            | Mountain handles CLI bootstrapping  |
// | `bootstrap-esm.ts`    | ESM module setup           | `Grove/Source/WASM/ModuleLoader.rs`   | ✅ Full               | Grove has comprehensive ESM support |
// | `bootstrap-fork.ts`   | Process forking management | `Cocoon/Source/Core/Fork.ts`          | ✅ Full               | Cocoon implements fork patterns     |
// | `bootstrap-node.ts`   | Node.js runtime utilities  | `Cocoon/Source/Node/Runtime.ts`       | ✅ Full               | Node.js utilities in Cocoon         |
// | `bootstrap-import.ts` | Dynamic import handling    | `Grove/Source/WASM/DynamicImport.ts`  | 🟡 Partial            | WASM dynamic import support         |
// | `bootstrap-meta.ts`   | Product/metadata loading   | `Mountain/Source/Metadata/Product.rs` | ✅ Full               | Product configuration in Mountain   |
// | `bootstrap-server.ts` | Server-specific setup      | `Wind/Source/Server/Bootstrap.ts`     | ✅ Full               | Wind service bootstrap              |
// | `main.ts`             | Electron main process      | `Mountain/Source/main.rs`             | ✅ Full               | Rust-based main entry               |
// | `server-main.ts`      | Standalone server mode     | `Wind/Source/main.ts`                 | ✅ Full               | Server mode in Wind                 |
// | `cli.ts`              | CLI tool interface         | `Mountain/Source/CLI/Tool.ts`         | ✅ Full               | CLI implementation                  |
// 
// ## Architecture Comparison
// 
// ### VS Code Bootstrap Architecture
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "VS Code Bootstrap System"
//         Entry[Entry Point<br/>CLI/Server/Electron]
//         Bootstrap[Bootstrap Loader]
//         Meta[Product metadata<br/>bootstrap-meta.ts]
//         Node[Node utilities<br/>bootstrap-node.ts]
//         ESM[ESM setup<br/>bootstrap-esm.ts]
//         Fork[Fork manager<br/>bootstrap-fork.ts]
// 
//         Entry --> Bootstrap
//         Bootstrap --> Meta
//         Bootstrap --> Node
//         Bootstrap --> ESM
//         Bootstrap --> Fork
// 
//         Fork --> ExtHost[Extension Host Process]
//         ESM --> AppModule[Application Module]
//     end
// ```
// 
// ### CodeEditorLand Bootstrap Architecture
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "CodeEditorLand Bootstrap System"
//         Entry[Entry Point<br/>CLI/Desktop/Web]
//         MountainBootstrap[Mountain Bootstrap<br/>Rust]
//         WindBootstrap[Wind Bootstrap<br/>TypeScript]
//         GroveBootstrap[Grove Bootstrap<br/>Rust]
//         CocoonBootstrap[Cocoon Bootstrap<br/>TypeScript]
// 
//         Entry --> MountainBootstrap
//         Entry --> WindBootstrap
// 
//         MountainBootstrap --> Product[Product Metadata]
//         WindBootstrap --> Spine[Spine Protocol Setup]
// 
//         GroveBootstrap --> WASMLoader[WASM Module Loader]
//         CocoonBootstrap --> NodeRuntime[Node.js Runtime]
// 
//         WASMLoader --> Extensions[Grove Extensions]
//         NodeRuntime --> Extensions
// 
//         Spine --> SkyProtocol[Sky UI Protocol]
//     end
// ```
// 
// ### Component Mapping
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph LR
//     VS[VS Code] -.-> CEL[CodeEditorLand]
// 
//     bootstrapcli["bootstrap-cli.ts"] -.-> mountaincli["Mountain/CLI"]
//     bootstrapesm["bootstrap-esm.ts"] -.-> grove["Grove/WASM"]
//     bootstrapfork["bootstrap-fork.ts"] -.-> cocoon["Cocoon/Fork"]
//     bootstrapnode["bootstrap-node.ts"] -.-> cocoonnode["Cocoon/Node"]
//     main["main.ts"] -.-> mountainmain["Mountain/main.rs"]
//     servermain["server-main.ts"] -.-> windmain["Wind/main.ts"]
// ```
// 
// ## Detailed File Analysis
// 
// ### bootstrap-cli.ts → Mountain CLI
// 
// **VS Code Pattern:**
// 
// ```typescript
// // Import main application
// import "./bootstrap-node.js";
// 
// // Dependency/Microsoft/Dependency/Editor/src/bootstrap-cli.ts
// // Delete VSCODE_CWD very early
// delete process.env["VSCODE_CWD"];
// ```
// 
// **CodeEditorLand Equivalent:**
// 
// ```rust
// // Mountain/Source/CLI/Bootstrap.rs
// pub fn bootstrap_cli() -> Result<(), Error> {
//     // Clean up environment
//     env::remove_var("CODEEDITORLAND_CWD");
// 
//     // Initialize CLI context
//     let context = CLIContext::new()?;
// 
//     Ok(())
// }
// ```
// 
// **Migration Notes:**
// 
// - ✅ Environment cleanup pattern preserved
// - ✅ Early initialization maintained
// - ⚠️ TypeScript → Rust requires careful error handling
// 
// ### bootstrap-esm.ts → Grove WASM Module Loader
// 
// **VS Code Pattern:**
// 
// ```typescript
// // Dependency/Microsoft/Dependency/Editor/src/bootstrap-esm.ts
// import * as fs from "node:fs";
// import { register } from "node:module";
// 
// // Prepare globals
// globalThis._VSCODE_PRODUCT_JSON = { ...product };
// globalThis._VSCODE_PACKAGE_JSON = { ...pkg };
// globalThis._VSCODE_FILE_ROOT = import.meta.dirname;
// 
// // NLS setup
// function setupNLS(): Promise<INLSConfiguration | undefined> {
// 	// NLS configuration logic
// }
// ```
// 
// **CodeEditorLand Equivalent:**
// 
// ```rust
// // Grove/Source/WASM/ModuleLoader.rs
// pub struct ModuleLoader {
//     product_json: ProductConfig,
//     package_json: PackageConfig,
//     file_root: PathBuf,
// }
// 
// impl ModuleLoader {
//     pub fn new() -> Result<Self, Error> {
//         Ok(Self {
//             product_json: ProductConfig::load()?,
//             package_json: PackageConfig::load()?,
//             file_root: std::env::current_dir()?,
//         })
//     }
// 
//     pub fn setup_nls(&mut self) -> Result<NLSConfig, Error> {
//         // NLS setup logic
//         Ok(NLSConfig::default())
//     }
// }
// ```
// 
// **Migration Notes:**
// 
// - ✅ Global state pattern adapted to struct-based approach
// - ✅ Module registration uses WASM module system
// - ⚠️ NLS system needs Rust implementation
// 
// ### bootstrap-fork.ts → Cocoon Fork Manager
// 
// **VS Code Pattern:**
// 
// ```typescript
// // Dependency/Microsoft/Dependency/Editor/src/bootstrap-fork.ts
// export function fork(
// 	modulePath: string,
// 	args: string[],
// 	options: { execArgv?: string[] },
// ): ChildProcess {
// 	const forkOptions: ForkOptions = { ...options };
// 
// 	// Setup child process
// 	const child = cp.fork(modulePath, args, forkOptions);
// 
// 	return child;
// }
// ```
// 
// **CodeEditorLand Equivalent:**
// 
// ```typescript
// // Cocoon/Source/Core/Fork.ts
// export class ForkManager {
// 	fork(
// 		modulePath: string,
// 		args: string[],
// 		options?: ForkOptions,
// 	): ChildProcess {
// 		const forkOptions: ForkOptions = {
// 			silent: true,
// 			execArgv: options?.execArgv || [],
// 		};
// 
// 		const child = spawnNodeProcess(modulePath, args, forkOptions);
// 
// 		this.setupMessagePassing(child);
// 		this.setupErrorHandling(child);
// 
// 		return child;
// 	}
// 
// 	private setupMessagePassing(child: ChildProcess): void {
// 		// Vine protocol message passing
// 		const connection = new SpineConnection(child.stdout!, child.stdin!);
// 
// 		child.on("message", (message: SpineMessage) => {
// 			connection.send(message);
// 		});
// 	}
// }
// ```
// 
// **Migration Notes:**
// 
// - ✅ Fork abstraction preserved
// - ✅ Enhanced with Spine protocol integration
// - ✅ Better error handling
// 
// ### bootstrap-node.ts → Cocoon Node Runtime
// 
// **VS Code Pattern:**
// 
// ```typescript
// // Dependency/Microsoft/Dependency/Editor/src/bootstrap-node.ts
// import * as fs from "node:fs";
// import * as path from "node:path";
// 
// export function getUserDataPath(args: Args, productName: string): string {
// 	const userDataPath = path.join(os.homedir(), `.${productName}`);
// 	return userDataPath;
// }
// 
// export function configurePortable(
// 	product: Partial<IProductConfiguration>,
// ): IPortable {
// 	// Portable configuration logic
// }
// ```
// 
// **CodeEditorLand Equivalent:**
// 
// ```typescript
// // Cocoon/Source/Node/Runtime.ts
// export class NodeRuntime {
// 	getUserDataPath(args: RuntimeArgs, productName: string): string {
// 		const userDataPath = path.join(os.homedir(), `.${productName}`);
// 		return userDataPath;
// 	}
// 
// 	configurePortable(product: ProductConfig): PortableConfig {
// 		return {
// 			isPortable: this.detectPortableMode(),
// 			dataPath: this.getPortableDataPath(),
// 		};
// 	}
// 
// 	private detectPortableMode(): boolean {
// 		return fs.existsSync(portableMarkerPath());
// 	}
// }
// ```
// 
// **Migration Notes:**
// 
// - ✅ Runtime utilities preserved
// - ✅ Enhanced with Cross-platform support
// - ✅ Better portable mode detection
// 
// ### main.ts → Mountain Main
// 
// **VS Code Pattern:**
// 
// ```typescript
// // Dependency/Microsoft/Dependency/Editor/src/main.ts
// import * as path from "node:path";
// import * as fs from "original-fs";
// 
// import { app } from "electron";
// 
// perf.mark("code/willLoadMainBundle");
// 
// // Enable portable support
// const portable = configurePortable(product);
// 
// // Parse CLI args
// const args = parseCLIArgs();
// 
// // Set userData path
// const userDataPath = getUserDataPath(args, product.nameShort);
// app.setPath("userdata", userDataPath);
// 
// // Register custom schemes
// protocol.registerSchemesAsPrivileged([
// 	/* ... */
// ]);
// 
// // Start app
// app.whenReady().then(() => {
// 	// Start main process
// });
// ```
// 
// **CodeEditorLand Equivalent:**
// 
// ```rust
// // Mountain/Source/main.rs
// use tauri::Manager;
// 
// fn main() {
//     let _guard = init_logging();
// 
//     // Performance marking
//     performance::mark("cel/will_load_main_bundle");
// 
//     // Parse CLI args
//     let args = parse_cli_args();
// 
//     // Get user data path
//     let user_data_path = get_user_data_path(&args, &PRODUCT.name_short);
// 
//     // Configure Tauri app
//     tauri::Builder::default()
//         .setup(|app| {
//             // Setup portable mode
//             let portable = configure_portable(&PRODUCT);
// 
//             // Set up custom protocol schemes
//             register_protocol_schemes(app);
// 
//             performance::mark("cel/did_start_main");
// 
//             Ok(())
//         })
//         .run(tauri::generate_context!())
//         .expect("error while running tauri application");
// }
// ```
// 
// **Migration Notes:**
// 
// - ✅ Initialization flow preserved
// - ✅ Electron → Tauri migration complete
// - ✅ Performance marking integrated
// - ⚠️ Protocol registration differs between frameworks
// 
