// # Integration Plans
// 
// This directory contains comprehensive documentation for integrating
// CodeEditorLand with existing systems and platforms, with a primary focus on
// Microsoft Visual Studio Code source integration.
// 
// ## 📑 Table of Contents
// 
// - [Overview](#overview)
// - [VS Code Integration](#vs-code-integration)
// - [Integration Types](#integration-types)
// - [Strategy](#strategy)
// - [Migration Guide](#migration-guide)
// - [Related Documentation](#related-documentation)
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// Integration documentation covers how CodeEditorLand can work with and migrate
// from existing code editor systems and platforms. Our primary focus is on
// Microsoft's Visual Studio Code, providing a comprehensive suite of tools and
// documentation for seamless integration and migration.
// 
// ### Integration Targets
// 
// | Target           | Type               | Status           | Documentation                 |
// | ---------------- | ------------------ | ---------------- | ----------------------------- |
// | **VS Code**      | Source Integration | ✅ Comprehensive | See VS Code Integration below |
// | **Atom**         | Migration          | ⏳ Future        | Planned                       |
// | **Vim/Neovim**   | Integration        | ⏳ Future        | Planned                       |
// | **Emacs**        | Integration        | ⏳ Future        | Planned                       |
// | **Sublime Text** | Migration          | ⏳ Future        | Planned                       |
// 
// ### VS Code Integration Status
// 
// | Component              | Status          | Documentation                                  |
// | ---------------------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
// | **Bootstrap System**   | 🟡 Mapped       | [`bootstrap-mapping.md`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/bootstrap-mapping.md) |
// | **API Compatibility**  | 🟡 65% Coverage | [`api-compatibility.md`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/api-compatibility.md) |
// | **Build System**       | 🟡 Mapped       | [`build-integration.md`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/build-integration.md) |
// | **Customization**      | 🟡 Mapped       | [`customization.md`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/customization.md)         |
// | **Source Integration** | 🟡 Planned      | [`vscode-source.md`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/vscode-source.md)         |
// 
// ## VS Code Integration
// 
// The VS Code integration plan provides comprehensive documentation for
// integrating with and migrating from Microsoft's Visual Studio Code source code.
// This includes detailed mappings of bootstrap files, API compatibility matrices,
// build system integration guides, and customization strategies.
// 
// ### Integration Documents
// 
// #### [`VS Code Source Integration`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/vscode-source.md)
// 
// Comprehensive guide for integrating with VS Code source code, including:
// 
// - Architecture comparison between VS Code and CodeEditorLand
// - Integration strategies (Monaco reuse, Extension API adapter, Workbench
//   architecture)
// - API mappings (Workspace, Window, Commands APIs)
// - Extension adapter implementation
// - Language Server Protocol integration
// 
// #### [`Bootstrap File Mapping`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/bootstrap-mapping.md)
// 
// Detailed mapping of VS Code bootstrap files to CodeEditorLand equivalents:
// 
// - Comprehensive bootstrap file mapping table
// - Architecture comparison diagrams
// - Detailed file analysis for each bootstrap file
// - Initialization flow sequences
// - Migration guide for bootstrap patterns
// 
// #### [`API Compatibility`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/api-compatibility.md)
// 
// Complete VS Code API implementation status matrix:
// 
// - Namespace coverage breakdown (window, workspace, commands, languages, etc.)
// - API implementation status (✅ Full, 🟡 Partial, ❌ Not implemented)
// - Extension compatibility analysis for popular extensions
// - API signature notes and compatibility considerations
// - Implementation timelines and progress tracking
// 
// #### [`Build System Integration`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/build-integration.md)
// 
// Comprehensive build system integration guide:
// 
// - Build command mapping table
// - Webpack → Vite migration guide
// - Module system adaptation (AMD → ESM)
// - Asset handling strategies
// - Code generation from protobuf files
// - Build optimization techniques
// 
// #### [`Customization Points`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/customization.md)
// 
// VS Code customization opportunities and migration:
// 
// - Product configuration field mappings
// - Theme customization with enhanced features
// - Extension marketplace integration
// - Telemetry system configuration
// - Authentication provider setup
// - Feature flag management
// - Localization support
// 
// ### Integration Architecture
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "VS Code Source"
//         VSC[VS Code Source]
//         Bootstrap[Bootstrap Files]
//         API[VS Code API]
//         Build[Build System]
//         Config[Product Config]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "CodeEditorLand Integration"
//         Mountain[Mountain Component]
//         Wind[Wind Component]
//         Grove[Grove Component]
//         Cocoon[Cocoon Component]
//         Sky[Sky Component]
//     end
// 
//     Bootstrap --> Mountain
//     Bootstrap --> Cocoon
//     API --> Cocoon
//     API --> Grove
//     Build --> Sky
//     Config --> Mountain
// 
//     style Mountain fill:#4CAF50
//     style Wind fill:#4CAF50
//     style Grove fill:#4CAF50
//     style Cocoon fill:#4CAF50
//     style Sky fill:#4CAF50
// ```
// 
// ## Integration Types
// 
// ### 1. Source Integration (VS Code Focus)
// 
// Integrate directly with VS Code source code:
// 
// - **Bootstrap System**: Map VS Code bootstrap files to Mountain, Cocoon, Grove
// - **API Implementation**: Implement VS Code API through Spine protocol
// - **Monaco Editor**: Direct reuse of Monaco editor component
// - **Extension Compatibility**: Run VS Code extensions via adapter layer
// 
// See [`Bootstrap Mapping`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/bootstrap-mapping.md) and
// [`API Compatibility`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/api-compatibility.md) for details.
// 
// ### 2. Migration
// 
// Migrate from VS Code codebase:
// 
// - **Configuration Migration**: Convert `settings.json` to CodeEditorLand config
// - **Extension Migration**: Adapt VS Code extensions to run on CodeEditorLand
// - **Theme Migration**: Convert VS Code themes with enhanced features
// - **User Data Transfer**: Migrate workspaces, keybindings, snippets
// 
// See [`Customization Points`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/customization.md) for configuration and theme
// migration guides.
// 
// ### 3. Coexistence
// 
// Run alongside VS Code:
// 
// - **Shared Workspaces**: Use same project configurations
// - **Extension Bridge**: Share extensions between editors
// - **Gradual Transition**: Migrate features incrementally
// 
// ### 4. Plugin Bridge
// 
// Run VS Code extensions:
// 
// - **Extension Host Compatibility**: Cocoon/Grove host VS Code extensions
// - **API Adapter**: Translate VS Code API calls to CodeEditorLand API
// - **Message Passing**: Use Spine protocol for extension communication
// 
// ## Strategy
// 
// ### VS Code Integration Strategy
// 
// ```mermaid
// flowchart TD
//     Start[Start VS Code Integration] --> Analyze[Analyze VS Code Source]
//     Analyze --> Map{Map Components}
// 
//     Map --> Bootstrap[Bootstrap Mapping]
//     Map --> API[API Compatibility]
//     Map --> Build[Build System]
//     Map --> Custom[Customization]
// 
//     Bootstrap --> Implement[Implement Integration]
//     API --> Implement
//     Build --> Implement
//     Custom --> Implement
// 
//     Implement --> Test[Integration Testing]
//     Test --> Validate[Validate Compatibility]
//     Validate --> Deploy[Deploy Integration]
// 
//     Deploy --> Migrate[Migrate Existing Data]
//     Migrate --> Extension[Migrate Extensions]
//     Extension --> Complete[Migration Complete]
// ```
// 
// ### Phase-Based Approach
// 
// | Phase                | Activities                           | Duration  | Deliverables                        |
// | -------------------- | ------------------------------------ | --------- | ----------------------------------- |
// | **Analysis**         | Study VS Code source, map components | 2-4 weeks | Component mapping documents         |
// | **Prototype**        | Build proof-of-concept for core APIs | 2-4 weeks | Working prototype, API adapter      |
// | **Implementation**   | Bootstrap, API, Build integration    | 4-8 weeks | Integrated components               |
// | **Testing**          | Comprehensive integration testing    | 2-4 weeks | Test coverage, compatibility matrix |
// | **Documentation**    | Developer and user documentation     | 1-2 weeks | Complete documentation              |
// | **Migration Tools**  | Build migration tooling              | 2-4 weeks | Migration scripts, converters       |
// | **Extension Bridge** | VS Code extension compatibility      | 4-8 weeks | Extension host adapter              |
// 
// ### Integration Roadmap
// 
// ```mermaid
// gantt
//     title VS Code Integration Roadmap
//     dateFormat  YYYY-MM-DD
//     section Phase 1: Analysis
//     Component Analysis        :2026-01-01, 30d
//     Bootstrap Mapping        :2026-01-15, 30d
// 
//     section Phase 2: Prototype
//     API Adapter Prototype    :2026-02-01, 30d
//     Monaco Integration       :2026-02-01, 20d
// 
//     section Phase 3: Implementation
//     Bootstrap System         :2026-02-15, 45d
//     Core APIs                :2026-02-15, 60d
//     Build System             :2026-03-01, 45d
// 
//     section Phase 4: Advanced
//     Extension Host           :2026-03-15, 60d
//     Language Services        :2026-03-15, 45d
//     Customization            :2026-04-01, 30d
// 
//     section Phase 5: Migration
//     Migration Tools          :2026-04-15, 30d
//     Extension Bridge         :2026-04-15, 45d
//     Testing & Validation     :2026-05-01, 30d
// ```
// 
// ## Migration Guide
// 
// ### VS Code to CodeEditorLand Quick Start
// 
// #### Step 1: Setup Environment
// 
// ```bash
// # Install CodeEditorLand CLI
// npm install -g @codeeditorland/cli
// 
// # Initialize new workspace
// cel init my-workspace
// cd my-workspace
// ```
// 
// #### Step 2: Migrate Configuration
// 
// ```bash
// # Migrate VS Code settings
// cel migrate:vscode settings \
// 	--from ~/.vscode/settings.json \
// 	--to .codeeditorland/config.toml
// 
// # Migrate keybindings
// cel migrate:vscode keybindings \
// 	--from ~/.vscode/keybindings.json \
// 	--to .codeeditorland/keybindings.json
// ```
// 
// #### Step 3: Migrate Extensions
// 
// ```bash
// # List installed VS Code extensions
// cel migrate:vscode:list-extensions
// 
// # Migrate compatible extensions
// cel migrate:vscode:extensions \
// 	--source ~/.vscode/extensions \
// 	--target .codeeditorland/extensions
// ```
// 
// #### Step 4: Migrate Themes
// 
// ```bash
// # Migrate custom themes
// cel migrate:vscode:theme \
// 	--path ~/.vscode/themes/my-theme.json \
// 	--output Theme/MyTheme/
// ```
// 
// ### Detailed Migration Guides
// 
// | Migration Type    | Document                                        | Status       |
// | ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |
// | **Configuration** | See [`Customization Points`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/customization.md)  | ✅ Available |
// | **Extensions**    | See [`API Compatibility`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/api-compatibility.md) | ✅ Available |
// | **Themes**        | See [`Customization Points`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/customization.md)  | ✅ Available |
// | **Bootstrap**     | See [`Bootstrap Mapping`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/bootstrap-mapping.md) | ✅ Available |
// | **Build System**  | See [`Build Integration`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/build-integration.md) | ✅ Available |
// 
// ### Conversion Examples
// 
// **Configuration Migration:**
// 
// ```typescript
// // VS Code settings.json
// {
//   "editor.tabSize": 4,
//   "editor.fontSize": 14,
//   "editor.wordWrap": "on",
//   "editor.minimap.enabled": true,
//   "workbench.colorTheme": "Dark+ (default)"
// }
// 
// // CodeEditorLand config.toml
// [editor]
// tab_size = 4
// font_size = 14
// word_wrap = true
// minimap_enabled = true
// 
// [ui]
// theme = "Dark+ (default)"
// ```
// 
// **Extension API Migration:**
// 
// ```typescript
// // VS Code extension API
// const vscode = require("vscode");
// 
// vscode.workspace.onDidChangeTextDocument((event) => {
// 	const document = event.document;
// 	const content = document.getText();
// 	console.log("Document changed:", content);
// });
// 
// // CodeEditorLand extension API (compatible)
// const vscode = require("vscode");
// 
// vscode.workspace.onDidChangeTextDocument((event) => {
// 	// Same API, works via adapter
// 	const document = event.document;
// 	const content = document.getText();
// 	console.log("Document changed:", content);
// });
// ```
// 
// **Theme Migration:**
// 
// ```json
// // VS Code theme -> CodeEditorLand theme (with enhancements)
// {
// 	"name": "My Theme",
// 	"type": "dark",
// 	// VS Code colors (fully supported)
// 	"colors": {
// 		"editor.background": "#1e1e1e",
// 		"editor.foreground": "#d4d4d4"
// 	},
// 	// CodeEditorLand enhancements
// 	"uiCustomizations": {
// 		"cssOverrides": "/* Custom CSS */",
// 		"iconThemes": { "dark": "vs-seti-dark" }
// 	}
// }
// ```
// 
// ### Migration Checklist
// 
// - [ ] Read [`Bootstrap Mapping`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/bootstrap-mapping.md) for bootstrap system
//       details
// - [ ] Review [`API Compatibility`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/api-compatibility.md) for supported features
// - [ ] Check [`Build Integration`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/build-integration.md) for build system
//       requirements
// - [ ] Review [`Customization Points`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/customization.md) for configuration
//       options
// - [ ] Migrate VS Code settings to CodeEditorLand config
// - [ ] Migrate custom themes with enhancements
// - [ ] Test extension compatibility
// - [ ] Run migration validation tools
// - [ ] Backup VS Code data before migration
// - [ ] Update team documentation with new workflows
