// # Standalone Architecture
// 
// Detailed architecture documentation for CodeEditorLand's standalone (web-only)
// mode.
// 
// ## 📑 Table of Contents
// 
// - [Overview](#overview)
// - [System Architecture](#system-architecture)
// - [Component Design](#component-design)
// - [Data Flow](#data-flow)
// - [Security Model](#security-model)
// - [Scaling Strategy](#scaling-strategy)
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// Standalone mode enables CodeEditorLand to run entirely in the browser without
// desktop dependencies, leveraging modern web technologies to provide a
// full-featured code editor experience.
// 
// ### Architecture Principles
// 
// | Principle                   | Description                   |
// | --------------------------- | ----------------------------- |
// | **Browser Native**          | Leverage browser capabilities |
// | **Progressive Enhancement** | Graceful degradation          |
// | **Offline First**           | PWA with offline support      |
// | **Cloud Ready**             | Designed for cloud deployment |
// | **Performance Oriented**    | Optimize for web performance  |
// 
// ## Core Services Architecture
// 
// Standalone mode provides web-native equivalents for Mountain's native services,
// enabling CodeEditorLand to run without the Tauri backend.
// 
// ### Standalone Services Interface
// 
// ```typescript
// // Standalone service equivalents
// interface StandaloneServices {
// 	// Replaces MountainFileSystemService
