// # Electron Desktop Deployment
// 
// Complete guide for packaging CodeEditorLand as a cross-platform desktop
// application using Electron.
// 
// ## 📑 Table of Contents
// 
// - [Overview](#overview)
// - [Architecture](#architecture)
// - [Configuration](#configuration)
// - [Main Process](#main-process)
// - [Renderer Process](#renderer-process)
// - [Native Integration](#native-integration)
// - [Building & Packaging](#building--packaging)
// - [Auto-Update](#auto-update)
// - [Code Signing](#code-signing)
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// Electron deployment provides a full-featured desktop application with native OS
// integration, enabling CodeEditorLand to offer a VS Code-like experience across
// Windows, macOS, and Linux.
// 
// ### Architecture Diagram
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "Electron App"
//         subgraph "Main Process"
//             App[App Main]
//             Window[BrowserWindow]
//             IPC[IPC Handler]
//             FileSys[Native FS]
//             Terminal[Terminal Process]
//             Menu[Menu Manager]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "Renderer Process"
//             SkyUI[Sky UI Layer]
//             Monaco[Monaco Editor]
//             Workers[Web Workers]
//             Preload[Preload Script]
//         end
// 
//         IPC <--> Preload
//         Window --> SkyUI
//         SkyUI --> Monaco
//         SkyUI --> Workers
//     end
// 
//     FileSys <--> IPC
//     Terminal <--> IPC
// 
//     OS[Operating System] --> App
//     App <--> OS
// ```
// 
// ## Configuration
// 
// ### Electron Builder Configuration
// 
