// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// plans/plans/standalone/README.md
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// # Standalone Mode
// 
// This directory contains documentation for CodeEditorLand's standalone mode - a
// web-only deployment option with no desktop dependencies.
// 
// ## 📑 Table of Contents
// 
// - [Overview](#overview)
// - [Deployment Models](#deployment-models)
// - [Architecture](#architecture)
// - [Configuration](#configuration)
// - [Performance](#performance)
// - [Roadmap](#roadmap)
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// Standalone mode enables CodeEditorLand to run purely in the browser without any
// desktop application or native dependencies. This enables cloud-based IDEs,
// online editors, and embedded code editing solutions.
// 
// ### Key Features
// 
// - ✅ Pure web deployment
// - ✅ No native dependencies
// - ✅ Cloud backend support
// - ✅ Offline capability with PWA
// - ✅ Real-time collaboration
// - ✅ CDN distribution
// 
// ### Design Goals
// 
// | Goal              | Description                        |
// | ----------------- | ---------------------------------- |
// | **Web-First**     | Optimized for browser environments |
// | **Cloud Native**  | Designed for cloud deployment      |
// | **Portable**      | No installation required           |
// | **Secure**        | Browser sandbox compliance         |
// | **Collaborative** | Real-time editing capabilities     |
// 
// ### Use Cases
// 
// | Scenario          | Description                           |
// | ----------------- | ------------------------------------- |
// | **Online IDE**    | Browser-based development environment |
// | **Code Editor**   | Embeddable code editor for websites   |
// | **Educational**   | Teaching and learning platform        |
// | **Documentation** | Interactive code examples             |
// | **Review**        | Code review tools                     |
// 
// ## Mode Variants
// 
// Standalone mode supports multiple deployment configurations based on the target
// environment and use case:
// 
// | Mode             | Backend             | Frontend                      | Transport        | Use Case                                   |
// | ---------------- | ------------------- | ----------------------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
// | **Browser-Only** | None (Web services) | Sky (Astro)                   | HTTP/WebSocket   | Browser access to hosted editor            |
// | **PWA**          | Service Worker      | Sky (Astro)                   | IndexedDB + HTTP | Offline-capable web app                    |
// | **Electron**     | Electron Main       | Sky (Astro + VSCode renderer) | IPC              | Desktop app (VS Code-like experience)      |
// | **Server-Only**  | Node.js server      | Sky (Astro)                   | WebSocket        | Remote development server                  |
// | **Cloud-Hosted** | Cloud backend       | Sky (Astro)                   | HTTPS            | Full cloud IDE with server-side processing |
// 
// ### Mode Details
// 
// #### Browser-Only Mode
// 
// - **Deployment**: Static hosting (Netlify, Vercel, GitHub Pages)
// - **Features**: Full editor, file management via IndexedDB, cloud sync optional
// - **Best For**: Quick access, demos, lightweight editing
// 
// #### PWA Mode
// 
// - **Deployment**: Static hosting with Service Worker
// - **Features**: Offline editing, sync when online, installable as app
// - **Best For**: Users with intermittent connectivity, mobile use
// 
// #### Electron Mode
// 
// - **Deployment**: Desktop application packages
// - **Features**: Native file system access, native terminal, native dialogs
// - **Best For**: Full IDE experience, power users, offline work
// 
// #### Server-Only Mode
// 
// - **Deployment**: Self-hosted Node.js server
// - **Features**: Remote development, server-side build tools, team workspaces
// - **Best For**: Development teams, CI/CD integration
// 
// #### Cloud-Hosted Mode
// 
// - **Deployment**: Cloud provider (AWS, GCP, Azure)
// - **Features**: Server-side processing, cloud storage, authentication,
//   collaboration
// - **Best For**: Cloud IDEs, education platforms, SaaS offerings
// 
// ## Deployment Models
// 
// ### 1. Static Web Hosting
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph LR
//     CDN[CDN] --> Files[Static Files]
//     Files --> Browser[User Browser]
// ```
// 
// **Characteristics:**
// 
// - Pure static hosting
// - No server processing
// - Client-side only
// - Fast deployment
// 
// **Hosting Options:**
// 
// - GitHub Pages
// - Netlify
// - Vercel
// - AWS S3 + CloudFront
// - Cloudflare Pages
// 
// ### 2. Server-Side Rendering (SSR)
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph LR
//     User[User Request] --> SSR[SSR Server]
//     SSR --> API[Backend API]
//     SSR --> Browser[Rendered HTML]
//     API --> Browser
// ```
// 
// **Characteristics:**
// 
// - Server-side rendering
// - API backend required
// - SEO friendly
// - Faster initial load
// 
// ### 3. Hybrid Mode
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "Client"
//         UI[UI Components]
//         PWAs[PWA Service]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Server"
//         API[REST GraphQL]
//         WebSocket[WebSocket Server]
//         Storage[Cloud Storage]
//     end
// 
//     UI <--> API
//     UI <--> WebSocket
//     PWAs <--> Storage
// ```
// 
// **Characteristics:**
// 
// - Best of both worlds
// - Offline capable
// - Real-time features
// - Cloud synchronization
// 
// ## Architecture
// 
// ### Component Architecture
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "Browser Client"
//         UI[Sky UI]
//         Wind[Wind Service]
//         WASM[WASM Extensions]
//         Cache[Browser Cache]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Network"
//         CDN[CDN]
//         API[API Gateway]
//         WebSocket[WebSocket]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Backend Services"
//         Grove[Grove WASM Host]
//         Air[Air Daemon Cloud]
//         Storage[File Storage]
//         Auth[Auth Service]
//     end
// 
//     UI --> Wind
//     Wind --> WASM
//     UI --> Cache
// 
//     Wind --> CDN
//     Wind --> API
//     Wind --> WebSocket
// 
//     API --> Grove
//     API --> Air
//     API --> Storage
//     API --> Auth
// ```
// 
// ### Data Flow
// 
// ```mermaid
// sequenceDiagram
//     participant User as User
//     participant UI as Sky UI
//     participant Cache as Browser Cache
//     participant API as Cloud API
//     participant Storage as Cloud Storage
// 
//     User->>UI: Open File
//     UI->>Cache: Check Cache
//     alt Cache Hit
//         Cache-->>UI: Cached Content
//         UI-->>User: Display
//     else Cache Miss
//         UI->>API: Request File
//         API->>Storage: Read File
//         Storage-->>API: File Content
//         API-->>UI: File Content
//         UI->>Cache: Update Cache
//         UI-->>User: Display
//     end
// ```
// 
// ### PWA Architecture
// 
// ```typescript
