// plans/plans/transport/common/error-handling.md
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// # Transport Error Handling
// 
// This document defines the comprehensive error handling strategy for the
// transport layer, including error taxonomy, codes, retry mechanisms, and circuit
// breaker patterns.
// 
// ## 📑 Table of Contents
// 
// - [Overview](#overview)
// - [Error Taxonomy](#error-taxonomy)
// - [Error Codes](#error-codes)
// - [Error Mapping](#error-mapping)
// - [Retry Strategies](#retry-strategies)
// - [Circuit Breaker Pattern](#circuit-breaker-pattern)
// - [Error Recovery](#error-recovery)
// - [Logging and Monitoring](#logging-and-monitoring)
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// Robust error handling is critical for a transport-layer agnostic system. This
// document provides a unified approach to handling errors across gRPC, IPC, and
// WASM transports.
// 
// ### Error Handling Principles
// 
// | Principle                | Description                                          |
// | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- |
// | **Fail Fast**            | Detect and surface errors quickly                    |
// | **Retry Smart**          | Use appropriate retry strategies based on error type |
// | **Graceful Degradation** | Fallback to alternative transports when possible     |
// | **Observable**           | All errors are logged with sufficient context        |
// | **Type Safe**            | Errors are strongly typed for programmatic handling  |
// 
// ## Error Taxonomy
// 
// Errors are categorized into three main levels: Transport, Protocol, and
// Application.
// 
// ### Error Taxonomy Diagram
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TD
//     A[Transport Errors] --> A1[Connection Errors]
//     A --> A2[Timeout Errors]
//     A --> A3[Network Errors]
// 
//     B[Protocol Errors] --> B1[Serialization Errors]
//     B --> B2[Deserialization Errors]
//     B --> B3[Validation Errors]
//     B --> B4[Version Mismatch Errors]
// 
//     C[Application Errors] --> C1[Business Logic Errors]
//     C --> C2[Permission Errors]
//     C --> C3[Resource Errors]
//     C --> C4[Rate Limit Errors]
// 
//     style A fill:#ff6b6b
//     style B fill:#feca57
//     style C fill:#48dbfb
// ```
// 
// ### Transport Errors
// 
// Errors related to the underlying transport mechanism (gRPC, IPC, WASM).
// 
// | Error Type             | Description                           | Retryable                |
// | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------ |
// | **Connection Refused** | Transport endpoint not available      | Yes, with backoff        |
// | **Connection Reset**   | Connection closed unexpectedly        | Yes                      |
// | **Connection Timeout** | Failed to establish connection        | Yes                      |
// | **Connection Lost**    | Connection established but lost       | Yes, after reconnect     |
// | **Socket Error**       | Low-level socket/network failure      | Yes                      |
// | **TLS Error**          | Certificate/TLS handshake failure     | No (requires config fix) |
// | **Resource Exhausted** | No available connections/file handles | No (scale required)      |
// 
// ### Protocol Errors
// 
// Errors related to message serialization, deserialization, and protocol
// compliance.
// 
// | Error Type                | Description                           | Retryable             |
// | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | --------------------- |
// | **Serialization Error**   | Failed to encode message              | No (data issue)       |
// | **Deserialization Error** | Failed to decode message              | No (data issue)       |
// | **Invalid Message**       | Message doesn't match schema          | No (data issue)       |
// | **Validation Error**      | Message fails validation rules        | No (data issue)       |
// | **Version Mismatch**      | Client/Server version incompatibility | No (upgrade required) |
// | **Checksum Error**        | Message corruption detected           | Yes (corruption)      |
// 
// ### Application Errors
// 
// Business logic errors returned by the application layer.
// 
// | Error Type              | Description                           | Retryable         |
// | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ----------------- |
// | **Invalid Argument**    | Request parameters are invalid        | No                |
// | **Not Found**           | Requested resource doesn't exist      | No                |
// | **Permission Denied**   | Client lacks required permissions     | No                |
// | **Rate Limited**        | Too many requests (429)               | Yes (after delay) |
// | **Resource Exhausted**  | Server resource limits reached (503)  | Yes (after delay) |
// | **Internal Error**      | Unexpected server error (500)         | Yes               |
// | **Service Unavailable** | Service temporarily unavailable (503) | Yes               |
// | **Operation Cancelled** | Request was cancelled                 | No                |
// 
// ## Error Codes
// 
// Unified error codes work across all transports and languages.
// 
// ### Error Code Structure
// 
// ```
// ┌─────┬─────┬──────┬────────────┐
// │ Cat │ Type│ Code │   Detail    │
// │(2b) │(2b) │ (3b) │    (7b)    │
// └─────┴─────┴──────┴────────────┘
// ```
// 
// - **Category (2 bits)**: 0=Transport, 1=Protocol, 2=Application
// - **Type (2 bits)**: Error sub-type
// - **Code (3 bits)**: Specific error code
// - **Detail (7 bits)**: Additional context
// 
// ### Error Code Registry
// 
// #### Transport Errors (Category 0x00)
// 
// | Code   | Hex  | Name                 | Retryable | Description            |
// | ------ | ---- | -------------------- | --------- | ---------------------- |
// | 0x0000 | 0x00 | `OK`                 | N/A       | Success                |
// | 0x0101 | 0x11 | `CONN_REFUSED`       | Yes       | Connection refused     |
// | 0x0102 | 0x12 | `CONN_TIMEOUT`       | Yes       | Connection timeout     |
// | 0x0103 | 0x13 | `CONN_RESET`         | Yes       | Connection reset       |
// | 0x0104 | 0x14 | `CONN_LOST`          | Yes       | Connection lost        |
// | 0x0201 | 0x21 | `READ_TIMEOUT`       | Yes       | Read timeout           |
// | 0x0202 | 0x22 | `WRITE_TIMEOUT`      | Yes       | Write timeout          |
// | 0x0203 | 0x23 | `REQUEST_TIMEOUT`    | Yes       | Request timeout        |
// | 0x0301 | 0x31 | `TLS_ERROR`          | No        | TLS handshake error    |
// | 0x0302 | 0x32 | `CERT_ERROR`         | No        | Certificate error      |
// | 0x0401 | 0x41 | `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` | No        | No available resources |
// 
// #### Protocol Errors (Category 0x40)
// 
// | Code   | Hex  | Name                    | Retryable | Description             |
// | ------ | ---- | ----------------------- | --------- | ----------------------- |
// | 0x4101 | 0x51 | `SERIALIZATION_ERROR`   | No        | Failed to serialize     |
// | 0x4102 | 0x52 | `DESERIALIZATION_ERROR` | No        | Failed to deserialize   |
// | 0x4103 | 0x53 | `CHECKSUM_ERROR`        | Yes       | Checksum mismatch       |
// | 0x4201 | 0x61 | `INVALID_MESSAGE`       | No        | Invalid message format  |
// | 0x4202 | 0x62 | `VALIDATION_ERROR`      | No        | Validation failed       |
// | 0x4301 | 0x71 | `VERSION_MISMATCH`      | No        | Version incompatibility |
// | 0x4302 | 0x72 | `UNKNOWN_METHOD`        | No        | Method not found        |
// 
// #### Application Errors (Category 0x80)
// 
// | Code   | Hex  | Name                  | Retryable | Description              |
// | ------ | ---- | --------------------- | --------- | ------------------------ |
// | 0x8101 | 0x91 | `INVALID_ARGUMENT`    | No        | Invalid parameters       |
// | 0x8102 | 0x92 | `OUT_OF_RANGE`        | No        | Parameter out of range   |
// | 0x8201 | 0xA1 | `NOT_FOUND`           | No        | Resource not found       |
// | 0x8202 | 0xA2 | `ALREADY_EXISTS`      | No        | Resource already exists  |
// | 0x8301 | 0xB1 | `PERMISSION_DENIED`   | No        | Insufficient permissions |
// | 0x8302 | 0xB2 | `UNAUTHENTICATED`     | No        | Not authenticated        |
// | 0x8401 | 0xC1 | `RATE_LIMITED`        | Yes       | Rate limit exceeded      |
// | 0x8501 | 0xD1 | `INTERNAL_ERROR`      | Yes       | Internal server error    |
// | 0x8502 | 0xD2 | `SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE` | Yes       | Service unavailable      |
// | 0x8503 | 0xD3 | `OPERATION_CANCELLED` | No        | Operation cancelled      |
// 
// ### HTTP Status Code Mapping
// 
// For transports that use HTTP (gRPC), error codes map to HTTP status codes:
// 
// | Error Category     | HTTP Status Range                      |
// | ------------------ | -------------------------------------- |
// | Transport Errors   | 502, 503, 504                          |
// | Protocol Errors    | 400, 415                               |
// | Application Errors | 400, 401, 403, 404, 409, 429, 500, 503 |
// 
// ## Error Mapping
// 
// Map transport-specific errors to unified error codes.
// 
// ### gRPC Status Mapping
// 
// ```rust
// // Rust: gRPC status to unified error code
// use tonic::Status;
// 
// pub fn map_grpc_status(status: &Status) -> ErrorCode {
//     match status.code() {
//         tonic::Code::Ok => ErrorCode::OK,
//         tonic::Code::Cancelled => ErrorCode::OPERATION_CANCELLED,
//         tonic::Code::InvalidArgument => ErrorCode::INVALID_ARGUMENT,
//         tonic::Code::DeadlineExceeded => ErrorCode::REQUEST_TIMEOUT,
//         tonic::Code::NotFound => ErrorCode::NOT_FOUND,
//         tonic::Code::AlreadyExists => ErrorCode::ALREADY_EXISTS,
//         tonic::Code::PermissionDenied => ErrorCode::PERMISSION_DENIED,
//         tonic::Code::ResourceExhausted => ErrorCode::RATE_LIMITED,
//         tonic::Code::FailedPrecondition => ErrorCode::INVALID_ARGUMENT,
//         tonic::Code::Aborted => ErrorCode::INTERNAL_ERROR,
//         tonic::Code::OutOfRange => ErrorCode::OUT_OF_RANGE,
//         tonic::Code::Unimplemented => ErrorCode::UNKNOWN_METHOD,
//         tonic::Code::Internal => ErrorCode::INTERNAL_ERROR,
//         tonic::Code::Unavailable => ErrorCode::SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE,
//         tonic::Code::DataLoss => ErrorCode::CHECKSUM_ERROR,
//         tonic::Code::Unauthenticated => ErrorCode::UNAUTHENTICATED,
//         _ => ErrorCode::INTERNAL_ERROR,
//     }
// }
// ```
// 
// ```typescript
// // TypeScript: gRPC status to unified error code
// export function mapGrpcStatus(status: {
// 	code: number;
// 	message: string;
// }): ErrorCode {
// 	const grpcToErrorCode: Record<number, ErrorCode> = {
// 		0: ErrorCode.OK,
// 		1: ErrorCode.OPERATION_CANCELLED,
// 		3: ErrorCode.INVALID_ARGUMENT,
// 		4: ErrorCode.REQUEST_TIMEOUT,
// 		5: ErrorCode.NOT_FOUND,
// 		6: ErrorCode.ALREADY_EXISTS,
// 		7: ErrorCode.PERMISSION_DENIED,
// 		8: ErrorCode.RATE_LIMITED,
// 		9: KeyCode.INVALID_ARGUMENT,
// 		10: ErrorCode.RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED,
// 		11: KeyCode.OUT_OF_RANGE,
// 		12: KeyCode.UNKNOWN_METHOD,
// 		13: ErrorCode.INTERNAL_ERROR,
// 		14: ErrorCode.SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE,
// 		15: ErrorCode.CHECKSUM_ERROR,
// 		16: ErrorCode.UNAUTHENTICATED,
// 	};
// 
// 	return grpcToErrorCode[status.code] ?? ErrorCode.INTERNAL_ERROR;
// }
// ```
// 
// ### IPC Error Mapping
// 
// ```rust
// // Rust: IPC-specific error mapping
// use std::io::Error as IoError;
// 
// pub fn map_ipc_error(error: &IoError) -> ErrorCode {
//     match error.kind() {
//         io::ErrorKind::ConnectionRefused => ErrorCode::CONN_REFUSED,
//         io::ErrorKind::ConnectionReset => ErrorCode::CONN_RESET,
//         io::ErrorKind::ConnectionAborted => ErrorCode::CONN_RESET,
//         io::ErrorKind::NotConnected => ErrorCode::CONN_LOST,
//         io::ErrorKind::BrokenPipe => ErrorCode::CONN_LOST,
//         io::ErrorKind::WouldBlock => ErrorCode::READ_TIMEOUT,
//         io::ErrorKind::TimedOut => ErrorCode::REQUEST_TIMEOUT,
//         _ => ErrorCode::INTERNAL_ERROR,
//     }
// }
// ```
// 
// ### WASM Error Mapping
// 
// ```typescript
// // TypeScript: WASM error code mapping
// export function mapWasmError(wasmCode: number): ErrorCode {
// 	const wasmToErrorCode: Record<number, ErrorCode> = {
// 		0: ErrorCode.OK,
// 		1: ErrorCode.CONN_REFUSED,
// 		2: ErrorCode.REQUEST_TIMEOUT,
// 		3: ErrorCode.SERIALIZATION_ERROR,
// 		4: ErrorCode.PROTOCOL_ERROR,
// 		99: ErrorCode.INTERNAL_ERROR,
// 	};
// 
// 	return wasmToErrorCode[wasmCode] ?? ErrorCode.INTERNAL_ERROR;
// }
// ```
// 
// ## Retry Strategies
// 
// Different error types require different retry strategies.
// 
// ### Retry Strategy Decision Tree
// 
// ```mermaid
// flowchart TD
//     A[Error Occurred] --> B{Is Retryable?}
//     B -->|No| C[Return Error Immediately]
//     B -->|Yes| D{Error Type?}
// 
//     D -->|Network/Connection| E[Exponential Backoff]
//     D -->|Rate Limit| F[Fixed Delay with Jitter]
//     D -->|Server Error 5xx| G[Linear Backoff]
//     D -->|Timeout| H[Exponential Backoff]
// 
//     E --> I{Max Retries Reached?}
//     F --> I
//     G --> I
//     H --> I
// 
//     I -->|Yes| C
//     I -->|No| J[Retry Request]
//     J --> A
// ```
// 
// ### Retry Strategies Matrix
// 
// | Strategy                 | Use Case                   | Backoff               | Jitter | Max Retries |
// | ------------------------ | -------------------------- | --------------------- | ------ | ----------- |
// | **None**                 | Non-retryable errors       | N/A                   | N/A    | 0           |
// | **Immediate**            | Transient network glitches | 0ms                   | N/A    | 1-2         |
// | **Fixed**                | Rate limiting              | 1000ms                | ±20%   | 3-5         |
// | **Linear**               | Server overload            | N+100ms               | ±10%   | 5-10        |
// | **Exponential**          | Connection issues          | 2^n × 100ms           | ±25%   | 3-7         |
// | **Exponential with Cap** | Persistent issues          | min(2^n × 100ms, 30s) | ±25%   | 10          |
// 
// ### Rust Retry Implementation
// 
// ```rust
// use tokio::time::{sleep, Duration};
// use rand::Rng;
// 
// #[derive(Debug, Clone)]
// pub struct RetryConfig {
//     pub max_attempts: u32,
//     pub initial_delay: Duration,
//     pub max_delay: Duration,
//     pub multiplier: f64,
//     pub jitter: f64, // 0.0 to 1.0
// }
// 
// impl Default for RetryConfig {
//     fn default() -> Self {
//         Self {
//             max_attempts: 3,
//             initial_delay: Duration::from_millis(100),
//             max_delay: Duration::from_secs(30),
//             multiplier: 2.0,
//             jitter: 0.25,
//         }
//     }
// }
// 
// pub async fn retry_with_backoff<F, T, E>(
//     config: &RetryConfig,
//     mut operation: F,
// ) -> Result<T, E>
// where
//     F: FnMut() -> Pin<Box<dyn Future<Output = Result<T, E>> + Send>>,
//     E: From<TransportError>,
// {
//     let mut delay = config.initial_delay;
//     let mut attempt = 0;
// 
//     loop {
//         attempt += 1;
// 
//         match operation().await {
//             Ok(result) => return Ok(result),
//             Err(e) => {
//                 if attempt >= config.max_attempts {
//                     return Err(e);
//                 }
// 
//                 // Add jitter
//                 let mut rng = rand::thread_rng();
//                 let jitter_amount = delay.as_millis() as f64 * config.jitter * (rng.gen::<f64>() - 0.5);
//                 let jitter_duration = Duration::from_millis(
//                     (delay.as_millis() as f64 + jitter_amount).max(0.0) as u64
//                 );
// 
//                 sleep(jitter_duration).await;
// 
//                 // Exponential backoff with cap
//                 delay = Duration::from_millis(
//                     (delay.as_millis() as f64 * config.multiplier)
//                         .min(config.max_delay.as_millis() as f64) as u64
//                 );
//             }
//         }
//     }
// }
// 
// // Usage example
// pub async fn send_with_retry<T>(
//     transport: &mut dyn TransportStrategy,
//     request: T,
// ) -> Result<T::Response, TransportError>
