// 
// ### Error Reporting Dashboard
// 
// Key metrics to monitor:
// 
// | Metric                            | Description                       | Alert Threshold |
// | --------------------------------- | --------------------------------- | --------------- |
// | `transport_requests_success_rate` | Percentage of successful requests | < 95%           |
// | `transport_request_latency_p99`   | 99th percentile latency           | > 1000ms        |
// | `transport_errors_rate`           | Errors per second                 | > 10/s          |
// | `transport_retries_rate`          | Retries per second                | > 5/s           |
// | `transport_circuit_breaker_state` | Circuit breaker state             | = 1 (Open)      |
// 
// ## Summary
// 
// The error handling strategy provides:
// 
// - **Comprehensive error taxonomy** for all error types
// - **Unified error codes** across all transports and languages
// - **Smart retry strategies** with configurable backoff and jitter
// - **Circuit breaker pattern** to prevent cascading failures
// - **Transport fallback** for automatic recovery
// - **Structured logging and metrics** for observability
// 
// This ensures robust error handling across gRPC, IPC, and WASM transports in
// CodeEditorLand.

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// plans/plans/transport/common/metrics.md
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// # Transport Metrics and Monitoring
// 
// This document defines the comprehensive metrics and monitoring strategy for the
// transport layer, including latency tracking, throughput monitoring, error rate
// monitoring, and health check endpoints.
// 
// ## 📑 Table of Contents
// 
// - [Overview](#overview)
// - [Metric Categories](#metric-categories)
// - [Latency Monitoring](#latency-monitoring)
// - [Throughput Monitoring](#throughput-monitoring)
// - [Error Rate Monitoring](#error-rate-monitoring)
// - [Connection Metrics](#connection-metrics)
// - [Health Check Endpoints](#health-check-endpoints)
// - [Grafana Dashboards](#grafana-dashboards)
// - [Alert Configuration](#alert-configuration)
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// Comprehensive monitoring is essential for maintaining transport layer
// reliability and performance. This document defines the metrics to collect, how
// to collect them, and how to use them for alerting and debugging.
// 
// ### Monitoring Principles
// 
// | Principle            | Description                                   |
// | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
// | **Observable**       | All transport operations emit metrics         |
// | **Queryable**        | Metrics are stored and can be queried         |
// | **Actionable**       | Alerts trigger based on meaningful thresholds |
// | **Contextual**       | Metrics include correlation IDs and metadata  |
// | **Minimal Overhead** | Metrics collection has <1% performance impact |
// 
// ### Metric Naming Conventions
// 
// ```
// <transport>_<resource>_<metric>_<unit>
// ```
// 
// Examples:
// 
// - `transport_grpc_request_duration_seconds` - gRPC request duration
// - `transport_ipc_messages_sent_total` - IPC messages sent
// - `transport_wasm_connection_errors_total` - WASM connection errors
// 
// Standard labels:
// 
// - `transport` - Transport type (grpc, ipc, wasm)
// - `method` - RPC method name
// - `status` - Status code (success or error code)
// - `peer` - Remote peer address
// - `component` - Component name (cocoon, grove, mountain, etc.)
// 
// ## Metric Categories
// 
// ### Category Overview
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TD
//     A[Transport Metrics] --> B[Latency Metrics]
//     A --> C[Throughput Metrics]
//     A --> D[Error Metrics]
//     A --> E[Connection Metrics]
//     A --> F[Resource Metrics]
//     A --> G[Business Metrics]
// 
//     style A fill:#48dbfb
//     style B fill:#1dd1a1
//     style C fill:#feca57
//     style D fill:#ff6b6b
//     style E fill:#ff9ff3
//     style F fill:#54a0ff
//     style G fill:#5f27cd
// ```
// 
// ### Metric Type Definitions
// 
// | Metric Type   | Description                    | Use Case                        |
// | ------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------- |
// | **Counter**   | Monotonically increasing value | Request counts, error counts    |
// | **Gauge**     | Can increase or decrease       | Active connections, queue sizes |
// | **Histogram** | Distribution of values         | Request latency, payload sizes  |
// | **Summary**   | Quantiles of a distribution    | Latency percentiles             |
// 
// ### All Metrics Registry
// 
// | Name                                        | Type      | Labels                          | Description           |
// | ------------------------------------------- | --------- | ------------------------------- | --------------------- |
// | `transport_request_duration_seconds`        | Histogram | transport, method, status       | Request latency       |
// | `transport_requests_total`                  | Counter   | transport, method, status, peer | Total requests        |
// | `transport_bytes_sent_total`                | Counter   | transport, peer                 | Bytes sent            |
// | `transport_bytes_received_total`            | Counter   | transport, peer                 | Bytes received        |
// | `transport_errors_total`                    | Counter   | transport, error_code, method   | Total errors          |
// | `transport_retries_total`                   | Counter   | transport, method               | Retry attempts        |
// | `transport_circuit_breaker_state`           | Gauge     | transport                       | Circuit breaker state |
// | `transport_active_connections`              | Gauge     | transport, peer                 | Active connections    |
// | `transport_connection_establishments_total` | Counter   | transport, peer, status         | Connection attempts   |
// | `transport_queue_depth`                     | Gauge     | transport                       | Request queue depth   |
// | `transport_payload_size_bytes`              | Histogram | transport, direction            | Payload sizes         |
// | `transport_health_score`                    | Gauge     | transport                       | Health score (0-100)  |
// 
// ## Latency Monitoring
// 
// Latency metrics measure the time from request initiation to response receipt.
// 
// ### Request Latency
// 
// **Metric:** `transport_request_duration_seconds`
// 
// **Type:** Histogram with buckets: [0.001, 0.005, 0.01, 0.025, 0.05, 0.1, 0.25,
// 0.5, 1, 2.5, 5, 10]
// 
// **Labels:**
// 
// - `transport` - grpc, ipc, wasm
// - `method` - RPC method name
// - `status` - success or error code
// - `component` - component name
// 
// **Example:**
// 
// ```promql
// # Average request latency by transport
// rate(transport_request_duration_seconds_sum[5m]) /
// rate(transport_request_duration_seconds_count[5m])
// 
// # P99 latency by method
// histogram_quantile(0.99,
//   sum(rate(transport_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m]))
//   by (le, method)
// )
// ```
// 
// ### Rust Implementation
// 
// ```rust
// use prometheus::{Histogram, HistogramOpts, HistogramVec};
// use once_cell::sync::OnceCell;
// 
// static REQUEST_LATENCY: OnceCell<HistogramVec> = OnceCell::new();
// 
// pub fn init_metrics() {
