// # IPC Transport
// 
// IPC (Inter-Process Communication) is the high-performance transport layer for
// CodeEditorLand, enabling fast, same-host communication between running
// processes.
// 
// ## 📑 Table of Contents
// 
// - [Overview](#overview)
// - [Architecture](#architecture)
// - [Protocol Definition](#protocol-definition)
// - [Implementation](#implementation)
// - [Configuration](#configuration)
// - [Security](#security)
// - [Performance](#performance)
// - [Roadmap](#roadmap)
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// IPC Transport provides the fastest communication channel for CodeEditorLand
// components running on the same host, leveraging native inter-process
// communication mechanisms of the operating system.
// 
// ### Key Features
// 
// - ✅ Native OS-level communication
// - ✅ Sub-millisecond latency
// - ✅ High throughput
// - ✅ Zero-copy capabilities (some platforms)
// - ✅ Automatic platform selection
// - ✅ Request/response pattern
// 
// ### Design Goals
// 
// | Goal               | Description                       |
// | ------------------ | --------------------------------- |
// | **Performance**    | Maximum speed and throughput      |
// | **Efficiency**     | Minimal CPU and memory overhead   |
// | **Reliability**    | Robust error handling             |
// | **Cross-Platform** | Support for Windows, macOS, Linux |
// | **Simplicity**     | Easy to use and integrate         |
// 
// ### Use Cases
// 
// | Scenario           | Description                            |
// | ------------------ | -------------------------------------- |
// | **Same-Process**   | In-process communication (thread-safe) |
// | **Local-Process**  | Communication between local processes  |
// | **High-Frequency** | Frequent, small messages               |
// | **Low-Latency**    | Time-critical operations               |
// 
// ## Architecture
// 
// ### Platform-Specific Implementations
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "IPC Transport"
//         Abstraction[IPC Abstraction Layer]
// 
//         subgraph "Windows"
//             NamedPipes[Named Pipes]
//             SharedMemory[Shared Memory]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "Unix/macOS"
//             UnixSockets[Unix Domain Sockets]
//             SharedMem[Shared Memory]
//             PosixMQ[POSIX Message Queue]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "In-Process"
//             Channels[builtin Channels]
//             SharedVars[Shared Variables]
//         end
//     end
// 
//     Abstraction --> NamedPipes
//     Abstraction --> UnixSockets
//     Abstraction --> Channels
//     Abstraction --> SharedMemory
//     Abstraction --> SharedMem
//     Abstraction --> PosixMQ
//     Abstraction --> SharedVars
// ```
// 
// ### Communication Flow
// 
// ```mermaid
// sequenceDiagram
//     participant Client as Client Process
//     participant IPC as IPC Layer
//     participant OS as OS IPC Mechanism
//     participant Server as Server Process
// 
//     Client->>IPC: Serialize Message
//     IPC->>OS: Send via IPC
//     OS->>Server: Deliver Message
//     Server->>Server: Process Message
//     Server->>OS: Send Response
//     OS->>IPC: Receive Response
//     IPC->>Client: Deserialize Response
// ```
// 
// ### Message Lifecycle
// 
// ```mermaid
// stateDiagram-v2
//     [*] --> Created: New Message
//     Created --> Serialized: Serialize
//     Serialized --> Queued: Queue for Send
//     Queued --> InTransit: Send via IPC
//     InTransit --> Received: OS Delivery
//     Received --> Deserialized: Parse
//     Deserialized --> Processed: Handle
//     Processed --> ResponseReady: Prepare Response
//     ResponseReady --> [*]: Response Sent
//     InTransit --> Failed: Error
//     Failed --> [*]: Return Error
// ```
// 
// ## Protocol Definition
// 
// ### IPC Message Format
// 
// ```typescript
// // IPC message structure
// export interface IpcMessage {
// 	header: IpcMessageHeader;
// 	body: Uint8Array;
// }
// 
// export interface IpcMessageHeader {
// 	// Message identification
// 	id: string;
// 	type: MessageType;
// 	correlationId?: string;
// 
// 	// Routing
// 	source: ProcessId;
// 	target: ProcessId;
// 
// 	// Metadata
// 	timestamp: number;
// 	size: number;
// 	flags: MessageFlags;
// }
// 
// export enum MessageType {
// 	REQUEST = 0,
// 	RESPONSE = 1,
// 	NOTIFICATION = 2,
// 	ERROR = 3,
// 	HEARTBEAT = 4,
// }
// 
// export interface MessageFlags {
// 	requireAck: boolean;
// 	highPriority: boolean;
// 	compressed: boolean;
// 	encrypted: boolean;
// }
// ```
// 
// ### Request/Response Protocol
// 
// ```typescript
// export interface IpcRequest extends IpcMessage {
// 	header: IpcMessageHeader & {
// 		type: MessageType.REQUEST;
// 	};
// 	body: IpcRequestBody;
// }
// 
// export interface IpcRequestBody {
// 	method: string;
// 	params: unknown;
// 	requestId: string;
// 	options: RequestOptions;
// }
// 
// export interface IpcResponse extends IpcMessage {
// 	header: IpcMessageHeader & {
// 		type: MessageType.RESPONSE;
// 		correlationId: string;
// 	};
// 	body: IpcResponseBody;
// }
// 
// export interface IpcResponseBody {
// 	success: boolean;
// 	result?: unknown;
// 	error?: IPCError;
// }
// 
// export interface IPCError {
// 	code: number;
// 	message: string;
// 	details?: unknown;
// }
// 
// export interface RequestOptions {
// 	timeout?: number;
// 	priority?: "low" | "normal" | "high";
// 	requireAck?: boolean;
// }
// ```
// 
