// plans/plans/transport/SUMMARY.md
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// # Transport-Layer Agnostic Abstraction - Implementation Summary
// 
// This document summarizes the comprehensive transport-layer agnostic abstraction
// design completed for CodeEditorLand, enabling all components to communicate via
// any transport mechanism (gRPC, IPC, WASM) through a unified Strategy pattern
// interface.
// 
// ## 📑 Overview
// 
// The transport-layer abstraction provides a unified, transport-agnostic interface
// that enables all CodeEditorLand components (Cocoon, Grove, Mountain, Air, Vine,
// Wind, Sky) to communicate seamlessly regardless of the underlying transport
// mechanism.
// 
// ### Key Achievements
// 
// ✅ **Created comprehensive common abstractions** for all transports  
// ✅ **Defined unified request/response model** across all languages  
// ✅ **Implemented error handling strategy** with taxonomy and retry logic  
// ✅ **Established serialization guidelines** for Protocol Buffers, MessagePack,
// and JSON  
// ✅ **Created metrics and monitoring** strategy with Prometheus integration  
// ✅ **Enhanced strategy pattern** with transport registry  
// ✅ **Added cross-language compatibility** tables and integration guides  
// ✅ **Developed decision trees** for automated transport selection  
// ✅ **Documented transport registry pattern** for dynamic transport management
// 
// ## 📁 Documentation Structure
// 
// ```
// plans/transport/
// ├── README.md                          # Transport system overview (enhanced)
// ├── strategy.md                        # Strategy pattern design (enhanced with registry)
// ├── decision-trees.md                  # Transport selection decision trees (new)
// ├── grpc.md                            # gRPC transport details
// ├── ipc.md                             # IPC transport details
// ├── wasm.md                            # WASM transport details
// └── common/                            # Common transport abstractions (new)
//     ├── README.md                      # Overview of common abstractions
//     ├── request-response.md            # Unified request/response model
//     ├── error-handling.md              # Error taxonomy and handling
//     ├── serialization.md               # Data serialization strategy
//     └── metrics.md                     # Transport metrics and monitoring
// ```
// 
// ## 🎯 Core Components
// 
// ### 1. Unified Transport Interface
// 
// All transports implement the same core interface:
// 
// ```rust
// #[async_trait]
// pub trait TransportStrategy {
//     type Request;
//     type Response;
//     type Error;
// 
//     async fn connect(&mut self) -> Result<(), Self::Error>;
//     async fn disconnect(&mut self) -> Result<(), Self::Error>;
//     async fn send_request(&mut self, request: Self::Request) -> Result<Self::Response, Self::Error>;
//     async fn send_notification(&mut self, notification: Notification) -> Result<(), Self::Error>;
//     async fn stream_events(&mut self) -> Result<Stream<Event>, Self::Error>;
// 
//     fn is_connected(&self) -> bool;
//     fn latency_ms(&self) -> u64;
// }
// ```
// 
// ### 2. Unified Request/Response Model
// 
// - **Protocol Buffers schema** for type-safe serialization
// - **Correlation ID handling** for request-response matching
// - **Timeout management** with configurable strategies
// - **Request lifecycle state machine** with tracking
// - **Streaming support** for real-time communication
// 
// ### 3. Error Handling Strategy
// 
// **Error Taxonomy:**
// 
// - **Transport Errors**: Connection, timeout, network failures
// - **Protocol Errors**: Serialization, deserialization, validation
// - **Application Errors**: Business logic, permissions, resource limits
// 
// **Unified Error Codes:**
// 
// - 0x00-0x7F: Transport errors
// - 0x80-0xBF: Protocol errors
// - 0xC0-0xFF: Application errors
// 
// **Retry Strategies:**
// 
// - Exponential backoff with jitter
// - Linear backoff for server overload
// - Fixed delay for rate limiting
// - Circuit breaker pattern for cascading failures
// 
// ### 4. Transport Registry
// 
// Dynamic transport selection and management:
// 
// ```rust
// pub struct TransportRegistry {
//     transports: HashMap<String, Box<dyn TransportStrategy>>,
//     active: Option<String>,
// }
// 
// impl TransportRegistry {
//     pub fn register(&mut self, name: String, transport: Box<dyn TransportStrategy>);
//     pub fn select(&mut self, name: &str) -> Result<&mut dyn TransportStrategy>;
//     pub fn get_active(&self) -> Option<&dyn TransportStrategy>;
//     pub fn list(&self) -> Vec<String>;
//     pub fn auto_select(&mut self, context: &TransportContext) -> Result<String>;
// }
// ```
// 
// ### 5. Serialization Strategy
// 
// **Format Comparison:**
// 
// | Feature     | Protocol Buffers                     | MessagePack  | JSON        |
// | ----------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------ | ----------- |
// | Size        | ⭐⭐⭐ Small (68% smaller than JSON) | ⭐⭐ Medium  | ⭐ Large    |
// | Speed       | ⭐⭐⭐ Fast                          | ⭐⭐⭐ Fast  | ⭐⭐ Medium |
// | Type Safety | ⭐⭐⭐ Strong                        | ⭐⭐ Dynamic | ⭐⭐ Weak   |
// | gRPC Native | ✅ Yes                               | ❌ No        | ❌ No       |
// 
// **Recommendations:**
// 
// - **gRPC/IPC**: Protocol Buffers (default)
// - **WASM**: Protocol Buffers with custom bridging
// - **Debugging/Logging**: JSON for readability
// 
// ### 6. Metrics and Monitoring
// 
// **Key Metrics:**
// 
// - `transport_request_duration_seconds` - Histogram
// - `transport_requests_total` - Counter
// - `transport_errors_total` - Counter
// - `transport_active_connections` - Gauge
// - `transport_circuit_breaker_state` - Gauge
// 
// **Health Check Endpoints:**
// 
// - `/health/transport` - Overall transport health
// - `/ready` - Readiness probe
// - `/live` - Liveness probe
// 
// ## 🔄 Cross-Language Support
// 
// ### Language Compatibility Matrix
// 
// | Feature             | Rust              | TypeScript       | WASM       |
// | ------------------- | ----------------- | ---------------- | ---------- |
// | **Transport Trait** | ✅ Native trait   | ✅ Interface     | ✅ Exports |
// | **Async/Await**     | ✅ Future         | ✅ Promise       | ✅ Promise |
// | **Serialization**   | ✅ Prost          | ✅ protobufjs    | ✅ Custom  |
// | **Metrics**         | ✅ Prometheus-rs  | ✅ prom-client   | ✅ Custom  |
// | **Streaming**       | ✅ Futures Stream | ✅ AsyncIterable | ✅ Stream  |
// 
// ### Component Transport Mapping
// 
// | Component    | Language    | Primary Transport | Secondary |
// | ------------ | ----------- | ----------------- | --------- |
// | **Cocoon**   | TypeScript  | gRPC              | WASM      |
// | **Grove**    | Rust + WASM | gRPC              | IPC       |
// | **Mountain** | Rust        | gRPC              | IPC       |
// | **Air**      | Rust        | gRPC              | IPC       |
// | **Wind**     | TypeScript  | gRPC              | WASM      |
// | **Sky**      | TypeScript  | WASM              | -         |
// 
// ## 📊 Transport Comparison
// 
// ### Feature Comparison
// 
// | Feature             | gRPC    | IPC       | WASM        |
// | ------------------- | ------- | --------- | ----------- |
// | **Bidirectional**   | ✅      | ✅        | ✅          |
// | **Streaming**       | ✅      | ❌        | ✅          |
// | **Binary Payload**  | ✅      | ✅        | ✅          |
// | **Zero-copy**       | Partial | ❌        | WASM memory |
// | **Type Safety**     | ✅      | ❌        | ✅          |
// | **Performance**     | High    | Very High | Medium      |
// | **Cross-language**  | ✅      | Limited   | Limited     |
// | **Connection Pool** | ✅      | ❌        | ❌          |
// 
// ### Performance Benchmarks
// 
// | Metric              | gRPC   | IPC     | WASM     |
// | ------------------- | ------ | ------- | -------- |
// | **Latency (P50)**   | 1-2ms  | <0.1ms  | 5-10ms   |
// | **Latency (P95)**   | 5-10ms | <0.5ms  | 50-100ms |
// | **Throughput**      | 10MB/s | 500MB/s | 1-5MB/s  |
// | **Memory Overhead** | 10MB   | 1MB     | 20MB     |
// 
// ## 🌲 Decision Trees
// 
// ### Automatic Selection Flow
// 
// ```mermaid
// flowchart TD
//     Start[Request] --> Environment{Environment?}
//     Environment --> Desktop[Desktop App]
//     Environment --> Web[Web App]
// 
//     Desktop --> Process{Same Process?}
//     Process --> Yes[Use IPC]
//     Process --> No[Use gRPC]
// 
//     Web --> Browser{Support WebSocket?}
//     Browser --> Yes[Use WASM + WebSocket]
//     Browser --> No[Use gRPC-Web]
// ```
// 
// ### Priority Order
// 
// | Priority | Desktop            | Web              |
// | -------- | ------------------ | ---------------- |
// | 1        | IPC                | WASM + WebSocket |
// | 2        | gRPC (Unix Socket) | gRPC-Web         |
// | 3        | gRPC (TCP)         | -                |
// 
// ## 🔧 Implementation Examples
// 
// ### Rust - Using Transport Registry
// 
// ```rust
// #[tokio::main]
// async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
//     let mut registry = TransportRegistry::new();
// 
//     // Register transports
//     let grpc_transport = GrpcTransport::new(GrpcConfig::default());
//     let ipc_transport = IpcTransport::new(IpcConfig::default());
// 
//     registry.register("grpc", grpc_transport);
//     registry.register("ipc", ipc_transport);
// 
//     // Auto-select based on environment
//     let context = TransportContext::detect();
//     let selected = registry.auto_select(&context)?;
// 
//     // Use the active transport
//     if let Some(transport) = registry.get_active() {
//         let request = UnifiedRequest::new("ping");
//         let response = transport.send_request(request).await?;
//     }
// 
//     Ok(())
// }
// ```
// 
// ### TypeScript - Using Transport Registry
// 
// ```typescript
// async function main() {
