// 		const request = { method: "ping", correlationId: generateId() };
// 		const response = await activeTransport.sendRequest(request);
// 	}
// }
// ```
// 
// ## 📋 Key Design Patterns
// 
// 1. **Strategy Pattern**: Dynamic transport selection based on context
// 2. **Registry Pattern**: Centralized transport management and switching
// 3. **Circuit Breaker Pattern**: Prevents cascading failures
// 4. **Retry Pattern**: Exponential backoff for transient errors
// 5. **Fallback Pattern**: Graceful degradation and failover
// 6. **Observer Pattern**: Metrics and event streaming
// 
// ## 🎓 Best Practices
// 
// ### Performance
// 
// - Use Protocol Buffers for best performance
// - Enable compression for payloads > 1KB
// - Use connection pooling where available
// - Batch small requests when possible
// 
// ### Reliability
// 
// - Implement retry for transient errors
// - Use circuit breaker to prevent cascading failures
// - Set appropriate timeouts based on SLAs
// - Monitor all metrics and set alerts
// 
// ### Security
// 
// - Use TLS for network transports
// - Validate all inputs before processing
// - Implement rate limiting on server side
// - Use secure defaults for all configurations
// 
// ### Debugging
// 
// - Include correlation IDs in all logs
// - Capture request/response payloads for debugging
// - Trace request lifecycles end-to-end
// - Use structured logging with consistent fields
// 
