// # 💨 Air: Background Daemon
// 
// Air is the background daemon service for CodeEditorLand, providing persistent
// backend services and background operations.
// 
// ## 📑 Table of Contents
// 
// - [Overview](#overview)
// - [Architecture](#architecture)
// - [Services](#services)
// - [Configuration](#configuration)
// - [Security](#security)
// - [Performance](#performance)
// - [Roadmap](#roadmap)
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// Air is a long-running background daemon that provides persistent services for
// CodeEditorLand, including indexing, caching, synchronization, and long-running
// background tasks.
// 
// ### Key Features
// 
// - ✅ Persistent background process
// - ✅ File indexing and search
// - ✅ Cache management
// - ✅ Task scheduling
// - ✅ Background job processing
// - ✅ Cross-platform daemon support
// 
// ### Design Goals
// 
// | Goal              | Description                              |
// | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
// | **Persistence**   | Maintain state across editor sessions    |
// | **Efficiency**    | Resource-efficient background operations |
// | **Scalability**   | Handle large projects efficiently        |
// | **Reliability**   | Graceful error handling and recovery     |
// | **Observability** | Comprehensive logging and monitoring     |
// 
// ### Use Cases
// 
// | Scenario          | Description                                    |
// | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
// | **File Indexing** | Build and maintain project file indexes        |
// | **Search**        | Fast content and file name search              |
// | **Caching**       | Cache frequently accessed data                 |
// | **Sync**          | Background synchronization with cloud services |
// | **Maintenance**   | Periodic cleanup and optimization tasks        |
// 
// ## Architecture
// 
// ### Component Design
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "Air Daemon"
//         subgraph "Core"
//             Scheduler[Task Scheduler]
//             JobQueue[Job Queue]
//             WorkerPool[Worker Pool]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "Services"
//             Indexer[File Indexer]
//             Search[Search Service]
//             Cache[Cache Manager]
//             Sync[Sync Service]
//             Cleanup[Cleanup Service]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "Storage"
//             Database[SQLite/PostgreSQL]
//             FileStore[File System Cache]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "Communication"
//             Vine[Vine Protocol Server]
//             Events[Event Bus]
//         end
//     end
// 
//     Scheduler --> JobQueue
//     JobQueue --> WorkerPool
//     WorkerPool --> Indexer
//     WorkerPool --> Search
//     WorkerPool --> Cache
//     WorkerPool --> Sync
//     WorkerPool --> Cleanup
// 
//     Indexer --> Database
//     Search --> Database
//     Cache --> FileStore
// 
//     Vine --> Scheduler
//     Vine --> Cache
// 
//     Indexer --> Events
//     Search --> Events
//     Cache --> Events
// ```
// 
// ### Startup Sequence
// 
// ```mermaid
// sequenceDiagram
//     participant OS as Operating System
//     participant Air as Air Daemon
//     participant Config as Config Service
//     participant Vine as Vine Server
//     participant Cache as Cache Manager
//     participant Indexer as File Indexer
// 
//     OS->>Air: Start Daemon
//     Air->>Config: Load Configuration
//     Config-->>Air: Configuration Loaded
//     Air->>Vine: Start Protocol Server
//     Vine-->>Air: Server Listening
//     Air->>Cache: Initialize Cache
//     Cache-->>Air: Cache Ready
//     Air->>Indexer: Start Indexing
//     Indexer-->>Air: Indexing Started
//     Air-->>OS: Daemon Ready
// ```
// 
// ### Job Processing Flow
// 
// ```mermaid
// flowchart LR
//     Submit[Job Submitted] --> Queue[Job Queue]
//     Queue --> Scheduler[Scheduler]
//     Scheduler --> Worker{Worker Available?}
//     Worker -->|Yes| Execute[Execute Job]
//     Worker -->|No| Wait[Wait in Queue]
//     Execute --> Result{Success?}
//     Result -->|Yes| Complete[Job Complete]
//     Result -->|No| Retry{Retry?}
//     Retry -->|Yes| Queue
//     Retry -->|No| Fail[Job Failed]
//     Complete --> Store[Store Result]
//     Fail --> Log[Log Error]
//     Wait --> Worker
// ```
// 
// ## Services
// 
