// # 🦋 Cocoon: Node.js Extension Host
// 
// Cocoon is the Node.js-based extension host for CodeEditorLand, providing a
// familiar JavaScript/TypeScript runtime for extensions.
// 
// ## 📑 Table of Contents
// 
// - [Overview](#overview)
// - [Architecture](#architecture)
// - [API Surface](#api-surface)
// - [Extension Development](#extension-development)
// - [Security](#security)
// - [Configuration](#configuration)
// - [Performance](#performance)
// - [Roadmap](#roadmap)
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// Cocoon provides a Node.js runtime environment for CodeEditorLand extensions,
// leveraging the vast npm ecosystem and familiar JavaScript/TypeScript development
// experience.
// 
// ### Key Features
// 
// - ✅ Full Node.js API support
// - ✅ npm package manager integration
// - ✅ TypeScript support out of the box
// - ✅ Hot-reload during development
// - ✅ Sandboxed execution environment
// - ✅ Extension compatibility with VS Code API
// 
// ### Design Goals
// 
// | Goal              | Description                                   |
// | ----------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
// | **Familiarity**   | Leverage existing VS Code extension knowledge |
// | **Ecosystem**     | Access to npm package registry                |
// | **Performance**   | Optimize for extension startup and execution  |
// | **Security**      | Safe execution of third-party code            |
// | **Compatibility** | Support VS Code extension API where possible  |
// 
// ### Use Cases
// 
// | Scenario              | Description                            |
// | --------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
// | **Language Services** | Linting, formatting, IntelliSense      |
// | **UI Extensions**     | Custom panels, views, status bar items |
// | **Tool Integration**  | Git, build tools, task runners         |
// | **Debugging**         | Custom debuggers, adapters             |
// | **Themes**            | Syntax highlighting, UI themes         |
// 
// ## Architecture
// 
// ### Component Design
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "Cocoon Extension Host"
//         subgraph "API Layer"
//             VSCodeAPI[VS Code API<br/>Compatibility Layer]
//             CELAPI[CodeEditorLand API<br/>Native Features]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "Extension Runtime"
//             Loader[Extension Loader]
//             Sandbox[Sandbox Environment]
//             Executor[Extension Executor]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "Communication Layer"
//             Vine[Vine Protocol]
//             Transports[Transport Adapters]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "Services"
//             Logger[Logging Service]
//             Config[Configuration Service]
//             Events[Event System]
//         end
//     end
// 
//     VSCodeAPI --> Executor
//     CELAPI --> Executor
//     Loader --> Sandbox
//     Sandbox --> Executor
//     Executor --> Vine
//     Vine --> Transports
//     Executor --> Logger
//     Executor --> Config
//     Executor --> Events
// ```
// 
// ### Extension Lifecycle
// 
// ```mermaid
// stateDiagram-v2
//     [*] --> Loading: Load Request
//     Loading --> Validating: Extension Loaded
//     Validating --> Activating: Validation Passed
//     Validating --> Error: Validation Failed
//     Activating --> Active: `activate()` Called
//     Active --> Deactivating: Deactivate Request
//     Deactivating --> Inactive: `deactivate()` Called
//     Inactive --> Unloading: Dispose
//     Unloading --> [*]
//     Error --> Unloading: Fatal Error
//     Active --> Error: Runtime Error
// ```
// 
// ### Request Flow
// 
// ```mermaid
// sequenceDiagram
//     participant UI as UI/Wind
//     participant Vine as Vine Protocol
//     participant API as API Layer
//     participant Ext as Extension
//     participant Sandbox as Sandbox
// 
//     UI->>Vine: Request
//     Vine->>API: Forward Request
//     API->>Sandbox: Execute in Context
//     Sandbox->>Ext: Call Extension Method
//     Ext-->>Sandbox: Return Result
//     Sandbox-->>API: Result
//     API-->>Vine: Response
//     Vine-->>UI: Response
// ```
// 
// ## API Surface
// 
// ### VS Code Compatibility Layer
// 
// Cocoon provides a compatibility layer for the VS Code API, enabling migration of
// existing extensions.
// 
// #### Supported APIs
// 
// | API Category | Status     | Notes                           |
// | ------------ | ---------- | ------------------------------- |
// | `workspace`  | ✅ Partial | File operations, events         |
// | `window`     | ✅ Partial | Status bar, notifications       |
// | `commands`   | ✅ Full    | Command registration, execution |
// | `languages`  | ✅ Partial | Diagnostic, completion          |
// | `env`        | ✅ Partial | Environment access              |
// | `extensions` | ✅ Full    | Extension management            |
// | `debug`      | 🔄 Planned | Debug adapter protocol          |
// | `scm`        | 🔄 Planned | Source control management       |
// 
// ### CodeEditorLand Native API
// 
// ```typescript
// // Core API Namespace
// namespace codeeditorland {
// 	// File System
// 	interface FileSystem {
// 		readFile(uri: string): Promise<Buffer>;
// 		writeFile(uri: string, content: Buffer): Promise<void>;
// 		deleteFile(uri: string): Promise<void>;
// 		listDirectory(uri: string): Promise<string[]>;
// 	}
// 
// 	// Process Control
// 	interface Process {
// 		execute(command: string, args: string[]): Promise<ProcessResult>;
// 		spawn(command: string, args: string[]): ProcessHandle;
// 	}
// 
// 	// UI Integration
// 	interface UI {
// 		showPanel(type: PanelType, content: string): void;
// 		setStatus(message: string): void;
// 		showNotification(message: string, type: NotificationType): void;
// 	}
// 
// 	// Configuration
// 	interface Configuration {
// 		get<T>(key: string): T | undefined;
// 		set<T>(key: string, value: T): void;
// 		watch(key: string, callback: (value: unknown) => void): Disposable;
// 	}
// 
// 	// Events
// 	interface EventService {
// 		on(event: string, callback: (...args: unknown[]) => void): Disposable;
// 		emit(event: string, ...args: unknown[]): void;
// 	}
// }
// ```
// 
