// # 🌲 Grove: Rust/WASM Extension Host
// 
// Grove is the Rust-based extension host for CodeEditorLand, providing
// high-performance extension execution with WebAssembly support.
// 
// ## 📑 Table of Contents
// 
// - [Overview](#overview)
// - [Architecture](#architecture)
// - [API Surface](#api-surface)
// - [Extension Development](#extension-development)
// - [Security](#security)
// - [Configuration](#configuration)
// - [Performance](#performance)
// - [Roadmap](#roadmap)
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// Grove provides a Rust runtime environment for CodeEditorLand extensions,
// leveraging Rust's performance, safety, and growing ecosystem. It also supports
// WebAssembly for cross-language extensions.
// 
// ### Key Features
// 
// - ✅ Native Rust performance
// - ✅ WebAssembly (WASM) support
// - ✅ Memory-safe execution
// - ✅ Zero-cost abstractions
// - ✅ Excellent tooling (Cargo, rust-analyzer)
// - ✅ Interop with Node.js extensions
// 
// ### Design Goals
// 
// | Goal                 | Description                                |
// | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
// | **Performance**      | Maximum execution speed and efficiency     |
// | **Safety**           | Memory and thread safety guarantees        |
// | **Portability**      | WASM for cross-platform extensions         |
// | **Interoperability** | Seamless integration with other components |
// | **Ecosystem**        | Leverage Cargo ecosystem                   |
// 
// ### Use Cases
// 
// | Scenario                 | Description                                   |
// | ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------- |
// | **Performance Critical** | Heavy computation, data processing            |
// | **WASM Extensions**      | C/C++, Rust, other languages compiled to WASM |
// | **Low-Level Access**     | System integration, native libraries          |
// | **High-Frequency**       | Language servers, real-time analysis          |
// | **Memory-Constrained**   | Efficient memory usage scenarios              |
// 
// ## Architecture
// 
// ### Component Design
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "Grove Extension Host"
//         subgraph "API Layer"
//             RustAPI[Rust Native API]
//             WASMAPI[WASM API Layer]
//             Interop[JS Interop Bridge]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "Extension Runtime"
//             RustLoader[Rust Extension Loader]
//             WASMLoader[WASM Runtime]
//             Sandbox[Sandbox Environment]
//             Executor[Extension Executor]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "Communication Layer"
//             Vine[Vine Protocol]
//             Transports[Transport Adapters]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "Services"
//             Logger[Logging Service]
//             Config[Configuration Service]
//             Events[Event System]
//         end
//     end
// 
//     RustAPI --> Executor
//     WASMAPI --> Executor
//     Interop --> Executor
//     RustLoader --> Sandbox
//     WASMLoader --> Sandbox
//     Sandbox --> Executor
//     Executor --> Vine
//     Vine --> Transports
//     Executor --> Logger
//     Executor --> Config
//     Executor --> Events
// ```
// 
// ### Extension Lifecycle
// 
// ```mermaid
// stateDiagram-v2
//     [*] --> Loading: Load Request
//     Loading --> Validating: Extension Loaded
//     Validating --> Compiling: WASM?
//     Validating --> Linking: Native?
//     Compiling --> Activating: WASM Compiled
//     Linking --> Activating: Native Linked
//     Activating --> Active: `activate()` Called
//     Active --> Deactivating: Deactivate Request
//     Deactivating --> Inactive: `deactivate()` Called
//     Inactive --> Unloading: Dispose
//     Unloading --> [*]
// ```
// 
// ### Request Flow
// 
// ```mermaid
// sequenceDiagram
//     participant UI as UI/Wind
//     participant Vine as Vine Protocol
//     participant API as API Layer
//     participant Ext as Extension
//     participant WASM as WASM Runtime
// 
//     UI->>Vine: Request
//     Vine->>API: Forward Request
//     API->>Ext: Call Extension Method
//     Ext->>WASM: WASM Function?
//     WASM-->>Ext: Result
//     Ext-->>API: Result
//     API-->>Vine: Response
//     Vine-->>UI: Response
// ```
// 
// ## API Surface
// 
// ### Rust Native API
// 
// ```rust
// // Core API traits
// pub trait Extension {
//     fn activate(&mut self, context: &ExtensionContext) -> Result<(), Error>;
//     fn deactivate(&mut self) -> Result<(), Error>;
// }
// 
// pub trait LanguageService {
//     fn complete(&self, params: CompletionParams) -> Vec<CompletionItem>;
//     fn hover(&self, params: HoverParams) -> Option<Hover>;
//     fn diagnostics(&self, params: DiagnosticParams) -> Vec<Diagnostic>;
// }
// 
// // File System API
// pub trait FileSystem {
//     fn read_file(&self, uri: &str) -> Result<Vec<u8>>;
//     fn write_file(&self, uri: &str, content: &[u8]) -> Result<()>;
//     fn delete_file(&self, uri: &str) -> Result<()>;
//     fn list_directory(&self, uri: &str) -> Result<Vec<String>>;
// }
// 
// // Process Control API
// pub trait Process {
//     fn execute(&self, command: &str, args: &[String]) -> Result<ProcessResult>;
//     fn spawn(&self, command: &str, args: &[String]) -> Result<ProcessHandle>;
// }
// 
// // UI Integration API
// pub trait UI {
//     fn show_panel(&self, panel_type: PanelType, content: &str) -> Result<()>;
//     fn set_status(&self, message: &str) -> Result<()>;
//     fn show_notification(&self, message: &str, notification_type: NotificationType) -> Result<()>;
// }
// 
// // Configuration API
// pub trait Configuration {
//     fn get<T>(&self, key: &str) -> Result<Option<T>>
//     where
//         T: DeserializeOwned;
//     fn set<T>(&self, key: &str, value: T) -> Result<()>
//     where
//         T: Serialize;
