// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// # Product Variants
// 
// This directory contains detailed specifications for each product variant in the
// CodeEditorLand architecture.
// 
// ## 📑 Table of Contents
// 
// - [Overview](#overview)
// - [Variant Categories](#variant-categories)
// - [Component Specifications](#component-specifications)
// - [Variant Relationships](#variant-relationships)
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// Product variants in CodeEditorLand represent different implementation approaches
// for each architectural component. Each variant can be combined with others to
// create complete product configurations.
// 
// ### Variant Symbol Reference
// 
// | Symbol | Component | Description              |
// | ------ | --------- | ------------------------ |
// | 🦋     | Cocoon    | Node.js Extension Host   |
// | 🌲     | Grove     | Rust/WASM Extension Host |
// | 🏔️     | Mountain  | Native Backend           |
// | 🌿     | Vine      | Protocol Definition      |
// | 💨     | Air       | Background Daemon        |
// | 🌬️     | Wind      | UI Service               |
// | ☁️     | Sky       | UI Components            |
// 
// ## Variant Categories
// 
// ### Extension Hosts
// 
// | Variant                                                                                     | Technology  | Primary Use Case                 |
// | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- | -------------------------------- |
// | [`Cocoon`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/variants/cocoon.md) 🦋 | Node.js     | JavaScript/TypeScript extensions |
// | [`Grove`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/variants/grove.md) 🌲   | Rust + WASM | Performance-critical extensions  |
// 
// ### Backend Components
// 
// | Variant                                                                                         | Technology   | Primary Use Case               |
// | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------ |
// | [`Mountain`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/variants/mountain.md) 🏔️ | Tauri + Rust | Desktop application backend    |
// | [`Air`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/variants/air.md) 💨           | Rust + async | Background services and daemon |
// 
// ### UI Components
// 
// | Variant                                                                                 | Technology         | Primary Use Case    |
// | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------- |
// | [`Sky`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/variants/sky.md) ☁️   | Astro + TypeScript | Modern web-based UI |
// | [`Wind`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/variants/wind.md) 🌬️ | Rust + WebAssembly | UI service layer    |
// 
// ### Protocol Layer
// 
// | Variant                                                                                 | Technology       | Primary Use Case                  |
// | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------- |
// | [`Vine`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/variants/vine.md) 🌿 | Protocol Buffers | Communication protocol definition |
// 
// ## Component Specifications
// 
// ### Core Characteristics
// 
// Each variant specification includes:
// 
// | Section                   | Description                            |
// | ------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
// | **Overview**              | High-level description and purpose     |
// | **Architecture**          | Internal architecture and design       |
// | **API Surface**           | Public and private APIs                |
// | **Dependencies**          | Required dependencies and integrations |
// | **Configuration**         | Configuration options and defaults     |
// | **Implementation Status** | Current development status             |
// | **Roadmap**               | Future plans and milestones            |
// | **Alternatives**          | Alternative approaches considered      |
// 
// ### Design Requirements
// 
// All variants must adhere to:
// 
// 1. **Protocol Compatibility**
//     - Must communicate via Vine protocol
//     - Support all transport options (gRPC, IPC, WASM)
//     - Implement proper error handling
// 
// 2. **Extensibility**
//     - Plugin architecture for extensions
//     - Clear extension points
//     - Stable public APIs
// 
// 3. **Security**
//     - Sandboxed extension execution
//     - Permission-based access control
//     - Secure data handling
// 
// 4. **Performance**
//     - Efficient resource usage
//     - Minimal latency
//     - Scalable architecture
// 
// 5. **Maintainability**
//     - Clear code organization
//     - Comprehensive documentation
//     - Extensive testing
// 
// ## Variant Relationships
// 
// ### Dependency Graph
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "Frontend Layer"
//         Sky[☁️ Sky]
//         Wind[🌬️ Wind]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Protocol Layer"
//         Vine[🌿 Vine]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Extension Layer"
//         Cocoon[🦋 Cocoon]
//         Grove[🌲 Grove]
//     end
// 
//     subgraph "Backend Layer"
//         Mountain[🏔️ Mountain]
//         Air[💨 Air]
//     end
// 
//     Sky --> Wind
//     Wind --> Vine
//     Vine --> Cocoon
//     Vine --> Grove
//     Cocoon --> Mountain
//     Grove --> Mountain
//     Mountain --> Air
// ```
// 
// ### Communication Matrix
// 
// | From     | To       | Protocol | Transport Options |
// | -------- | -------- | -------- | ----------------- |
// | Sky      | Wind     | Vine     | IPC, gRPC         |
// | Wind     | Cocoon   | Vine     | IPC, gRPC         |
// | Wind     | Grove    | Vine     | gRPC, WASM        |
// | Cocoon   | Mountain | Vine     | IPC, gRPC         |
// | Grove    | Mountain | Vine     | IPC, gRPC         |
// | Mountain | Air      | Vine     | IPC, gRPC         |
// 
// ### Compatibility Matrix
// 
// | Variant  | Compatible With    | Notes                      |
// | -------- | ------------------ | -------------------------- |
// | Cocoon   | Mountain, Air      | Primary extension host     |
// | Grove    | Mountain, Air      | Performance extension host |
// | Mountain | Cocoon, Grove, Air | Backend for desktop        |
// | Air      | Cocoon, Grove      | Background services        |
// | Sky      | Wind               | UI frontend                |
// | Wind     | Cocoon, Grove      | UI mediation               |
// | Vine     | All                | Universal protocol         |
// 
// ## Implementation Status Summary
// 
// | Variant     | Status     | Priority |
// | ----------- | ---------- | -------- |
// | 🦋 Cocoon   | ✅ Active  | High     |
// | 🌲 Grove    | 🔄 Planned | Medium   |
// | 🏔️ Mountain | ✅ Active  | High     |
// | 🌿 Vine     | ✅ Active  | High     |
// | 💨 Air      | 🔄 Planned | Medium   |
// | 🌬️ Wind     | 🔄 Planned | Medium   |
// | ☁️ Sky      | ✅ Active  | High     |
// 
// ### Status Legend
// 
// - ✅ **Active**: Fully implemented and maintained
// - 🔄 **Planned**: Approved and in development queue
// - ⏳ **Proposed**: Under consideration
// - 📊 **Reference**: Legacy or reference implementation
// 
// ## Implementation Guidelines
// 
// ### When to Choose Each Variant
// 
// #### Cocoon vs Grove
// 
// | Factor             | Cocoon                | Grove                |
// | ------------------ | --------------------- | -------------------- |
// | **Language**       | JavaScript/TypeScript | Rust                 |
// | **Performance**    | Good                  | Excellent            |
// | **Ecosystem**      | Large npm             | Growing crates.io    |
// | **Learning Curve** | Low                   | Medium               |
// | **Use Case**       | General extensions    | Performance-critical |
// 
// #### Mountain vs Standalone
// 
// | Factor          | Mountain        | Standalone |
// | --------------- | --------------- | ---------- |
// | **Platform**    | Desktop (Tauri) | Web        |
// | **File Access** | Native          | Limited    |
// | **Performance** | Native          | Web        |
// | **Deployment**  | Installer       | Web server |
// 
// #### Sky vs VS Code UI
// 
// | Factor            | Sky   | VS Code UI        |
// | ----------------- | ----- | ----------------- |
// | **Technology**    | Astro | Monaco + Electron |
// | **Performance**   | Fast  | Slower            |
// | **Customization** | High  | Medium            |
// | **Compatibility** | New   | VS Code API       |
// 
// ## Testing Strategy
// 
// Each variant requires:
// 
// 1. **Unit Tests**
//     - Core functionality
//     - Edge cases
//     - Error handling
// 
// 2. **Integration Tests**
//     - Protocol communication
//     - Cross-component integration
//     - End-to-end flows
// 
// 3. **Performance Tests**
//     - Latency measurements
//     - Resource usage
//     - Load handling
// 
// 4. **Compatibility Tests**
//     - Transport compatibility
//     - Version compatibility
//     - Platform compatibility
// 
// ## Documentation Standards
// 
// Each variant document must include:
// 
// - ✅ Clear overview and purpose
// - ✅ Architecture diagrams (Mermaid)
// - ✅ API documentation
// - ✅ Configuration options
// - ✅ Usage examples
// - ✅ Development guidelines
// - ✅ Testing requirements
// - ✅ Migration notes (if applicable)
// 
// ## Contributing
// 
// When adding or modifying a variant:
// 
// 1. Review existing variant specifications
// 2. Ensure protocol compatibility
// 3. Document all changes
// 4. Update this README
// 5. Update the
//    [`combinatorics matrix`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/combinatorics/matrix.md)
// 6. Add appropriate tests
// 
// ## Related Documentation
// 
// - [`Architecture Overview`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/overview.md)
// - [`Transport Strategies`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/transport/)
// - [`Product Combinatorics`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/combinatorics/matrix.md)
// - [`Integration Plans`](https://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land/tree/Current/plans/integration/)
