// # 🌬️ Wind: UI Service
// 
// Wind is the UI service layer for CodeEditorLand, providing mediation between the
// frontend UI and backend services.
// 
// ## 📑 Table of Contents
// 
// - [Overview](#overview)
// - [Architecture](#architecture)
// - [API Surface](#api-surface)
// - [Component Integration](#component-integration)
// - [Configuration](#configuration)
// - [Performance](#performance)
// - [Roadmap](#roadmap)
// 
// ## Overview
// 
// Wind serves as the UI service layer for CodeEditorLand, acting as a mediator
// between the Sky frontend and backend services (Mountain, Cocoon, Grove). It
// handles request routing, caching, and UI-specific logic.
// 
// ### Key Features
// 
// - ✅ UI request routing and mediation
// - ✅ Client-side caching
// - ✅ State management
// - ✅ Event handling and broadcasting
// - ✅ Real-time updates
// - ✅ Responsive UI coordination
// 
// ### Design Goals
// 
// | Goal                 | Description                                   |
// | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
// | **Mediation**        | Act as intermediary between UI and backend    |
// | **Caching**          | Reduce backend requests through smart caching |
// | **State Management** | Maintain consistent UI state                  |
// | **Reactivity**       | Enable real-time UI updates                   |
// | **Performance**      | Minimize latency and improve responsiveness   |
// 
// ### Use Cases
// 
// | Scenario              | Description                               |
// | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
// | **Request Routing**   | Route UI requests to appropriate services |
// | **Caching**           | Cache frequently accessed data            |
// | **State Sync**        | Synchronize state across UI components    |
// | **Event Handling**    | Handle and broadcast UI events            |
// | **Real-time Updates** | Push updates to UI components             |
// 
// ## Architecture
// 
// ### Component Design
// 
// ```mermaid
// graph TB
//     subgraph "Wind UI Service"
//         subgraph "Request Layer"
//             Router[Request Router]
//             Validator[Request Validator]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "Service Layer"
//             Cache[Cache Manager]
//             State[State Manager]
//             Event[Event Bus]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "Transport Layer"
//             VineClient[Vine Client]
//             StreamManager[Stream Manager]
//         end
// 
//         subgraph "UI Integration"
//             Adapter[UI Adapter]
//             Hooks[React Hooks/API]
//         end
//     end
// 
//     Router --> Validator
//     Validator --> Cache
//     Cache --> VineClient
//     VineClient --> StreamManager
// 
//     Router --> State
//     State --> Event
//     Event --> Adapter
// 
//     Cache --> Event
//     StreamManager --> Event
// 
//     Adapter --> Hooks
// ```
// 
// ### Request Flow
// 
// ```mermaid
// sequenceDiagram
//     participant UI as Sky UI
//     participant Wind as Wind Service
//     participant Cache as Cache
//     participant Vine as Vine Client
//     participant Backend as Backend Service
// 
//     UI->>Wind: Request
//     Wind->>Cache: Check Cache?
//     alt Cache Hit
//         Cache-->>Wind: Cached Data
//         Wind-->>UI: Response
//     else Cache Miss
//         Wind->>Vine: Forward Request
//         Vine->>Backend: Send Request
//         Backend-->>Vine: Response
//         Vine-->>Wind: Response
//         Wind->>Cache: Update Cache
//         Wind-->>UI: Response
//     end
// ```
// 
// ### Event Flow
// 
// ```mermaid
// flowchart LR
//     Source[Event Source] --> Filter{Event Filter?}
//     Filter -->|Pass| Bus[Event Bus]
//     Filter -->|Block| Drop[Drop]
//     Bus --> Subscriber1[Subscriber 1]
//     Bus --> Subscriber2[Subscriber 2]
//     Bus --> Cache[Cache Invalidation]
//     Bus --> State[State Update]
// ```
// 
