// # Workbench Loading Investigation & Implementation Plan
// 
// **Date**: 2026-02-13 **Status**: Investigation Complete **Priority**: Critical
// 
// ---
// 
// ## Executive Summary
// 
// This document provides a comprehensive analysis of how the VSCode Electron
// workbench loads in VSCode and proposes implementation strategies for adapting it
// to work in Code Editor Land's Tauri environment. The investigation covers:
// 
// 1. Current Output package structure and build configuration
// 2. Electron vs Browser workbench variants
// 3. Architecture of Mountain, Wind, Cocoon, and Air components
// 4. Electron-to-VSCode communication patterns
// 5. Recommended implementation approaches (low-friction vs high-frigration)
// 6. Detailed implementation roadmaps
// 
// ---
// 
// ## Table of Contents
// 
// - [1. Current Situation](#1-current-situation)
// - [2. VSCode Build Configuration Analysis](#2-vscode-build-configuration-analysis)
// - [3. Workbench Variants Comparison](#3-workbench-variants-comparison)
// - [4. Architecture Deep Dive](#4-architecture-deep-dive)
// - [5. Electron-to-VSCode Communication](#5-electron-to-vscode-communication)
// - [6. Implementation Approaches](#6-implementation-approaches)
// - [7. Low-Friction Implementation Plan](#7-low-friction-implementation-plan)
// - [8. High-Frigration Implementation Plan](#8-high-frigration-implementation-plan)
// - [9. Recommendations](#9-recommendations)
// - [10. Next Steps](#10-next-steps)
// 
// ---
// 
// ## 1. Current Situation
// 
// ### 1.1 Current Error
// 
// ```
// Refused to load vscode-file://vscode-app/file:///app/out/vs/workbench/workbench.desktop.main.js
// because it does not appear in the script-src directive of the Content Security Policy.
// ```
// 
// **Root Cause**: The VSCode Electron workbench uses the `vscode-file://`
// protocol, which is Electron-specific and doesn't exist in Tauri/web
// environments.
// 
// ### 1.2 Current Implementation
// 
// **File**:
// [`Element/Sky/Source/Workbench/Default.astro`](../../Element/Sky/Source/Workbench/Default.astro)
// 
// ```typescript
// // Loads Electron workbench
// import "@codeeditorland/output/vs/code/electron-browser/workbench/workbench.js";
// ```
// 
// The file attempts to:
// 
// 1. Install Wind preload polyfill (via
//    [`@codeeditorland/wind/Target/Function/Install.js`](../../Element/Wind/Source/Function/Install.ts))
// 2. Load VSCode Electron workbench
// 
// This fails because:
// 
// - Electron workbench expects `vscode-file://` protocol
// - Electron-specific APIs (`ipcRenderer`, `process`, etc.) are not available in
//   Tauri
// - Workbench expects native file system access without gRPC intermediaries
// 
// ### 1.3 Available Workbench Alternatives
// 
// | Variant         | Location                     | Status       | Description                                       |
// | --------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------- |
// | **Electron**    | `Default.astro`              | ❌ Fails     | VSCode Electron workbench, requires Electron APIs |
// | **Browser**     | `Browser.astro`              | ✅ Available | VSCode browser workbench, web-compatible          |
// | **Native Wind** | `Native/WindWorkbench.astro` | ✅ Complete  | Custom workbench using Wind services              |
// | **Wind**        | `Wind.astro`                 | ⚠️ Unclear   | Another Wind-based variant                        |
// 
// ---
// 
// ## 2. VSCode Build Configuration Analysis
// 
// ### 2.1 Output Package Build Configuration
// 
// **File**:
// [`Element/Output/Source/ESBuild/Microsoft/VSCode.ts`](../../Element/Output/Source/ESBuild/Microsoft/VSCode.ts)
// 
// **Key Findings**:
// 
// ```typescript
// export const Prefix = `out${!On ? "-build" : ""}/vs`;
// 
// entryPoints: (await import("@playform/build/Target/Function/Entry.js")).default(
// 	Current,
// 	[
// 		// ...
// 		...(await import("../Exclude/Workbench.js").default(Prefix)),
// 		// ...
// 	],
// );
// ```
// 
// **Platform**: `browser` (line 138)
// 
// **Important**: The build targets `browser` platform, but the exclusion logic
// determines which workbench files are included.
// 
// ### 2.2 Bundling Configuration
// 
// **File**:
// [`Element/Output/Source/ESBuild/Microsoft/VSCode/Bundle.ts`](../../Element/Output/Source/ESBuild/Microsoft/VSCode/Bundle.ts)
// 
// **External Dependencies** (includes `electron`):
// 
// ```typescript
// external: [
// 	"electron", // Line 67 - Electron is marked as external
// 	// ... many other native dependencies
// ];
// ```
// 
// **Key Discovery**: Electron is marked as external, meaning:
// 
// - ESBuild will not bundle Electron code
// - Workbench code expects `require('electron')` to be available
// - In Tauri, this will fail unless polyfilled
// 
// ### 2.3 Built Output Structure
// 
// ```
// Element/Output/Target/Microsoft/VSCode/
// ├── vs/code/
// │   ├── browser/workbench/workbench.js      ← Browser workbench ✅
// │   └── electron-browser/workbench/workbench.js  ← Electron workbench ❌
// ├── vs/workbench/
// │   ├── browser/workbench.js                ← Core workbench logic
// │   ├── browser/web.main.js                 ← Browser main entry
// │   └── electron-browser/desktop.main.js    ← Electron main entry
// ```
// 
// **Critical Finding**: Both browser and Electron variants exist in the built
// output!
// 
