// #### Phase 3: Extend Mountain IPC Handlers (Week 2)
// 
// **File**:
// [`Element/Mountain/Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers.rs`](../../Element/Mountain/Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers.rs)
// 
// These handlers already exist! We just need to ensure they support all VSCode
// file system operations.
// 
// **Key Operations Needed**:
// 
// - `file:read` - ✅ Already exists
// - `file:write` - ✅ Already exists
// - `file:stat` - ✅ Already exists
// - `file:delete` - ✅ Already exists
// - `file:mkdir` - ✅ Already exists
// - `file:readdir` - ✅ Already exists
// - `file:copy` - ✅ Already exists
// - `file:move` - ✅ Already exists
// 
// **Verification Required**: Check that these handlers return data in the format
// VSCode expects.
// 
// #### Phase 4: Update Sky Routing (Week 2)
// 
// **File**:
// [`Element/Sky/Source/pages/Application.astro`](../../Element/Sky/Source/pages/Application.astro)
// or similar routing file
// 
// Update to use the new Tauri workbench:
// 
// ```typescript
// // Change from Default.astro to Tauri.astro
// import Workbench from "../Workbench/Tauri.astro";
// ```
// 
// #### Phase 5: Testing & Refinement (Week 3)
// 
// **Test Cases**:
// 
// 1. ✅ Workbench loads without CSP errors
// 2. ✅ File system operations work (read, write, delete)
// 3. ✅ Configuration is loaded from Mountain
// 4. ✅ Editor opens and displays files
// 5. ✅ Basic editing and saving works
// 
// **Debugging**:
// 
// - Add detailed logging in MountainProxy
// - Monitor Tauri IPC traffic
// - Verify Mountain service responses
// 
// ### 7.4 Known Risks & Mitigation
// 
// | Risk                                             | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation                                     |
// | ------------------------------------------------ | ---------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------------- |
// | Browser workbench hardcoded to use remote agent  | Medium     | High   | Implement proxy layer before provider override |
// | VSCode expects specific response formats         | Medium     | Medium | Map Mountain responses to VSCode format        |
// | File system providers not easily interchangeable | Low        | High   | Create custom provider implementation          |
// | Configuration access patterns differ             | Low        | Medium | Intercept configuration service calls          |
// 
// ### 7.5 Success Criteria
// 
// - [ ] VSCode browser workbench loads successfully
// - [ ] File explorer displays directory contents
// - [ ] Files can be opened in the editor
// - [ ] File edits can be saved
// - [ ] Configuration is loaded from Mountain
// - [ ] No CSP errors in console
// - [ ] Performance is acceptable (<2s load time)
// 
// ---
